1
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:07,000
T LIVING
TOGETHER, AND THEY HAVE A CHILD

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:09,000
AND THEY SORT OF BECOME NORMAL.

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:10,000
HE GOES TO WORK.

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:15,000
HE'S NO LONGER THE ROMANTIC
R.A.F. DASHING PILOT FIGURE.

5
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:18,000
SHE HAS LOST HER INDEPENDENCE
TO SOME EXTENT.

6
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:21,000
SHE IS NOT ALLOWED TO WORK.

7
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:23,000
SHE USED TO BE A NURSE
DURING THE WAR--

8
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:26,000
AT LEAST, A VOLUNTEER NURSE.

9
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,000
WELL, THAT'S NOT THE THING TO DO

10
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:31,000
IF YOU'RE A RESPECTABLE
MARRIED WOMAN

11
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:34,000
OF THE UPPER MIDDLE CLASS
IN BRITAIN IN THE 1920s

12
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:38,000
SO SHE IS AT HOME
DEALING WITH THE SERVANTS

13
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:41,000
DEALING WITH THE CHILD
TO A LIMITED EXTENT.

14
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:44,000
SHE'S LIVING THE LIFE
OF THE ORDINARY MATRON.

15
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:45,000
HE TAKES TO GOLF.

16
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:49,000
HE SPENDS HIS TIME INCREASINGLY
ON THE GOLF COURSE.

17
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:51,000
SHE STARTED OFF LIKING GOLF

18
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:54,000
BUT SHE DOESN'T LIKE
GOLF THAT MUCH.

19
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:56,000
SHE'S A GOLF WIDOW.

20
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:59,000
THE TWO OF THEM
START TO HAVE LITTLE..

21
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:01,000
LESS AND LESS IN COMMON.

22
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:05,000
THAT'S TO SAY, THEIR INITIAL
LACK OF COMMON INTERESTS

23
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:07,000
BECOMES A MAJOR ISSUE
BETWEEN THEM

24
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:09,000
AND SO THEY DRIFT APART

25
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:14,000
AND EVENTUALLY
HE FINDS SOMEONE ELSE.

26
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:21,000
Captioned by
The Caption Center
WGBH Educational Foundation

27
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:26,000
MYSTERY! IS MADE
POSSIBLE BY A GRANT

28
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:35,000
FROM MOBIL CORPORATION,
WHICHERE, LOOK OUT, GUV!K

29
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:40,000
WHOA!

30
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:45,000
MY DEAR MR. SHAW,
ARE YOU ALL RIGHT?

31
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:47,000
YES... YES,
I THINK SO.

32
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:50,000
HERE, HE DONE
THAT ON PURPOSE.

33
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:52,000
HE WAS TRYING
TO KILL YOU!

34
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:55,000
Poirot:
AN ATTEMPTED
MURDER...

35
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:57,000
AMERICAN
LIBERTY BONDS...

36
00:01:57,000 --> 00:01:58,000
HAVE THEY
BEEN ROBBED?

37
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:00,000
NOT YET, MISS LEMON.

38
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:04,000
BUT THEY THINK
THAT THEY ARE GOING TO BE.

39
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:05,000
AND WHEN THEY ARE

40
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:09,000
THERE IS AT STAKE THE SUM
OF ONE MILLION DOLLARS.

41
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:13,000
( thunder )

42
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:15,000
MYSTERY! IS MADE POSSIBLE

43
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:20,000
BY A GRANT
FROM MOBIL CORPORATION.

44
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:30,000
CAPTIONING OF THIS PROGRAM
IS MADE POSSIBLE

45
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:32,000
BY THE CORPORATION
FOR PUBLIC BROADCASTING

46
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:34,000
AND PUBLIC TELEVISION STATIONS.

47
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:39,000
( thunder )

48
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:42,000
( crack )

49
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:47,000

( woman wailing )

50
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:56,000
HERCULE POIROT ABHORS SHIPS.

51
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:58,000
HE CAN'T SAIL THE ROLLING WAVES

52
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:01,000
WITHOUT GETTING
DREADFULLY SEASICK.

53
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:03,000
BUT MAL DE MER ISN'T
THE WORST OF IT

54
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:05,000
FOR THE METICULOUS BELGIAN.

55
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:08,000
AFTER ALL, HOW DOES
ONE MAINTAIN ONE'S DIGNITY

56
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:10,000
WHILE LURCHING ABOUT ON DECK?

57
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:15,000
BUT POIROT'S PASSION FOR ORDER,
GASTROLOGICAL AND OTHERWISE

58
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:19,000
MUST SOMETIMES TAKE SECOND PLACE
TO DUTY, AS IT DOES TONIGHT

59
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:23,000
WHEN THE DETECTIVE ESCORTS
A SHIPMENT OF LIBERTY BONDS

60
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:24,000
ACROSS THE SEA.

61
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:28,000
IT'S FITTING THAT THE WORLD'S
GREATEST DETECTIVE

62
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:32,000
SHOULD SAIL ABOARD THE WORLD'S
GREATEST SHIP, THE QUEEN MARY:

63
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:34,000
LARGEST LINER OF HER DAY.

64
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:37,000
SO LARGE, IN FACT,
THAT PASSENGERS OFTEN GOT LOST.

65
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:40,000
BUT THEY ALWAYS MANAGED
TO NAVIGATE A COURSE

66
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:43,000
TO THE SHIP'S
REMARKABLE RESTAURANT

67
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:45,000
WHICH CONTAINED
A CAPTAIN'S BRIDGE

68
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:47,000
AND A FIVE-TIER DECK.

69
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:49,000
DINERS COULD SIP DRINKS
IN DECK CHAIRS

70
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:53,000
OR DANCE IN A SALON
THAT LOOKED LIKE A GIANT RAFT

71
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:56,000
WHILE THE ORCHESTRA PLAYED
FROM LIFEBOATS.

72
00:03:56,000 --> 00:04:00,000
BUT TONIGHT, YOU WON'T
FIND POIROT REVELING

73
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:03,000
WITH HIS 1,900
FELLOW PASSENGERS.

74
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:07,000
HE'S MORE CONCERNED
WITH GUARDING HIS VALUABLE CARGO

75
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:09,000
UNTIL IT ARRIVES
SAFELY IN NEW YORK.

76
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:11,000
AND A GOOD THING, TOO.

77
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:15,000
FOR EVEN AS THE QUEEN MARY
STEAMS OUT OF SOUTHAMPTON

78
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:16,000
ON HER MAIDEN VOYAGE

79
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:19,000
A MODERN-DAY PIRATE IS PLOTTING

80
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:24,000
"THE MILLION DOLLAR
BOND ROBBERY."

81
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:27,000
MORNING,
MR. SHAW.

82
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:32,000
MORNING,
MR. VAVASOUR.

83
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:41,000
Vavasour:
TERRIBLE WEATHER,
MR. SHAW.

84
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:46,000
Shaw:
YES, SHOCKING.

85
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:59,000
I'LL SEE YOU AT
THE BANK, MR. SHAW.

86
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:00,000
RIGHT,
MR. VAVASOUR.

87
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:01,000
MORNING, GUV.

88
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:06,000
MORNING.

89
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:17,000
( engine starts )

90
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:20,000
HERE, LOOK OUT, GUV!

91
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:25,000
WHOA!

92
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:29,000
Vavasour:
MY DEAR MR. SHAW,
ARE YOU ALL RIGHT?

93
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:32,000
YES... YES,
I THINK SO.

94
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:35,000
HERE, HE DONE
THAT ON PURPOSE!

95
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:40,000
HE WAS TRYING
TO KILL YOU!

96
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:47,000
Hastings:
IT WEIGHS 80,000 TONS, YOU KNOW.

97
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:51,000
THAT IS HEAV HASTINGS.

98
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:54,000
IT'S OVER
A THOUSAND FEET LONG.

99
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:57,000
YES, HASTINGS.

100
00:07:57,000 --> 00:08:01,000
ITS SIREN CAN BE HEARD
TEN MILES AWAY.

101
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:02,000
TEN MILES, POIROT!

102
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:04,000
AH, MON DIEU.

103
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:05,000
I'D GIVE MY
EYE TEETH

104
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:07,000
TO BE ON THIS
MAIDEN VOYAGE.

105
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:09,000
IT'S AN
ENGINEERING MARVEL.

106
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:11,000
IT IS A MARVEL TO ME
HOW ANYONE WISHES

107
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:13,000
TO TRAVEL ON
SUCH A CONTRAPTION.

108
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:14,000
CONTRAPTION?

109
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:15,000
THE QUEEN MARY?

110
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:18,000
POIROT, YOU'RE
GOING TOO FAR.

111
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:20,000
NO, HASTINGS,
I'M GOING NOWHERE.

112
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:23,000
TO CONTEMPLATE SUCH A MATTER
GIVES ME MAL DE MER.

113
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:24,000
I CAN ASSURE
YOU, POIROT

114
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:26,000
YOU WOULDN'T
BE SEASICK

115
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:27,000
ON THE
QUEEN MARY.

116
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:29,000
STEADY AS A ROCK.

117
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:32,000
HASTINGS, 20 YEARS AGO
I CAME TO THIS COUNTRY

118
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:36,000
IN A BOAT ACROSS THE CHANNEL,
AND STILL I AM NOT RECOVERED.

119
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:37,000
Miss Lemon:
MR. POIROT

120
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:41,000
THIS JUST CAME FOR YOU
BY PERSONAL MESSENGER.

121
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:44,000
THANK YOU,
MISS LEMON.

122
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:46,000
THE LONDON AND SCOTTISH BANK.

123
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:48,000
DO WE HAVE

124
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:49,000
AN ACCOUNT
THERE?

125
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:50,000
NO.

126
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:52,000
MR. POIROT
HAD PROBLEMS
WITH HIS BANK.

127
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:55,000
THE CHAIRMAN
WAS ARRESTED.

128
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:56,000
YES, I REMEMBER.

129
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:58,000
IT WAS POIROT WHO PUT
THE MAN BEHIND BARS.

130
00:08:58,000 --> 00:09:00,000
THIS IS MOST UNUSUAL.

131
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:02,000
INDEED A CIRCUMSTANCE UNIQUE.

132
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:05,000
AN ATTEMPTED
MURDER...

133
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:08,000
AMERICAN
LIBERTY BONDS...

134
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:09,000
HAVE THEY
BEEN ROBBED?

135
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:11,000
NOT YES, MISS LEMON.

136
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:14,000
BUT THEY THINK THAT
THEY ARE GOING TO BE.

137
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:16,000
AND WHEN THEY ARE

138
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:21,000
THERE IS AT STAKE THE SUM
OF ONE MILLION DOLLARS.

139
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:44,000
MR. POIROT, ARE YOU AWARE
OF THE NATURE OF LIBERTY BONDS?

140
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:46,000
I HAVE NO PERSONAL
EXPERIENCE.

141
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:49,000
THEY'RE THE EQUIVALENT
OF BLANK CHECKS

142
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:51,000
PAYABLE TO WHOEVER
HOLDS THEM.

143
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:54,000
AND IF THEY
WERE MISLAID?

144
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:59,000
SAME AS LOSING CASH--
IT WOULD RUIN US.

145
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:01,000
TELL ME,
MONSIEUR SHAW

146
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:03,000
WHY IS IT
NECESSARY

147
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:05,000
TO TRANSPORT
THESE BONDS?

148
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:06,000
THE BANK IS
EXTENDING ITS CREDIT

149
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:08,000
IN AMERICA,
MR. POIROT.

150
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:10,000
WE MUST HAVE
FUNDS IN PLACE
IN NEW YORK.

151
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:11,000
PLEASE...

152
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:16,000
THANK YOU.

153
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:18,000
AND IT IS
MONSIEUR SHAW

154
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:20,000
WHO WILL TAKE THEM?

155
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:21,000
YES, IN TWO
DAYS' TIME.

156
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:23,000
HE'LL TRAVEL ON
THE QUEEN MARY.

157
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:26,000
I SAY!

158
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:28,000
OH, SORRY...

159
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:32,000
NOW, IF MONSIEUR SHAW WERE
UNABLE TO MAKE THIS JOURNEY

160
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:34,000
WHO WOULD TRAVEL IN HIS PLACE?

161
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:37,000
THE ASSISTANT GENERAL
MANAGER, MR. RIDGEWAY.

162
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:39,000
BUT MR. RIDGEWAY IS
ABOVE SUSPICION.

163
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:41,000
I WOULD LIKE TO THINK SO.

164
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:43,000
Poirot:
WHY IS THAT,
MONSIEUR VAVASOUR?

165
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:46,000
HE'S BEEN WITH THE BANK
FOR SEVEN YEARS.

166
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:47,000
HE'S ALSO ENGAGED

167
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:52,000
TO MY
SECRETARY.

168
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:58,000
YES, GENTLEMAN, I WILL
EXAMINE THIS MATTER FOR YOU.

169
00:10:58,000 --> 00:11:00,000
REALLY, MR. VAVASOUR...

170
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:02,000
NO, MR. SHAW, THAT
CAR TRIED TO KILL YOU.

171
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:04,000
I SAW IT WITH
MY OWN EYES.

172
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:06,000
Poirot:
THE RED
SPORTS CAR.

173
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:07,000
A SINGER, YOU THINK.

174
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:09,000
UH, YES...

175
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:13,000
Poirot:
BUT YOU WERE
UNABLE TO MAKE OUT

176
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:14,000
THE REGISTRATION
NUMBER?

177
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:16,000
IT HAPPENED TOO QUICKLY.

178
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:18,000
IN TRUTH, MY EYESIGHT
IS NOT GOOD.

179
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:21,000
I THINK YOU'RE BLOWING
THIS OUT OF PROPORTION.

180
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:24,000
WE'LL LET MR. POIROT
BE THE JUDGE OF THAT.

181
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:26,000
YOU'D BETTER
HAVE A WORD

182
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:29,000
WITH OUR MR. McNEIL,
THE HEAD OF SECURITY.

183
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:30,000
I'M SURE YOU'LL FIND HIM

184
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:35,000
MORE THAN
HELPFUL.

185
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:37,000
I TELL YOU,
MR. POIROT

186
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:39,000
I CONSIDER YOUR
PRESENCE HERE

187
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:40,000
AN INTRUSION
IN MY AFFAIRS.

188
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:43,000
THAT IS FOR MONSIEUR
VAVASOUR TO DECIDE.

189
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:45,000
I'LL HAVE YOU KNOW
IN THE FIVE YEARS

190
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:47,000
I'VE BEEN HEAD
OF SECURITY HERE

191
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:49,000
NOT A PAPER CLIP
HAS GONE ASTRAY.

192
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:50,000
MONSIEUR McNEIL,
I'M SURE

193
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:52,000
IF SUCH A THING
WERE TO HAPPEN

194
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:57,000
YOU WOULD BE THE MAN
IDEAL FOR THE CASE.

195
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:16,000

HERE IT IS,
MR. POIROT.

196
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:18,000
THE PORTMANTEAU IN WHICH
THE BONDS WILL TRAVEL.

197
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:21,000
I HAD IT BUILT
TO MY OWN DESIGN:

198
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:25,000
STEEL PLATE INSIDE, FIVE-
LEVER LOCK, HARDENED STEEL

199
00:12:25,000 --> 00:12:29,000
CLUTCH SCREWS
HERE AND HERE.

200
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:31,000
McNeil:
THERE ARE JUST THREE KEYS.

201
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:32,000
ONE FOR MR. SHAW

202
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:37,000
AND ONE FOR
MR. VAVASOUR.

203
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:40,000
AND THE THIRD?

204
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:45,000
FOR ME, OF COURSE.

205
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:48,000
AND WHAT IF MONSIEUR RIDGEWAY
HAD TO MAKE THE JOURNEY?

206
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:49,000
MR. RIDGEWAY?

207
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:51,000
BS
THAT'S THE BANK'S LOOKOUT

208
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:55,000
BUT I HAVE TO SAY HE WOULD NOT
BE MY FIRST CHOICE AS COURIER.

209
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:58,000
AND WHY IS THAT,
MONSIEUR McNEIL?

210
00:12:58,000 --> 00:13:02,000
YOU'RE THE DETECTIVE,
MR. POIROT.

211
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:07,000
YOU WORK IT OUT.

212
00:13:23,000 --> 00:13:25,000
THANK YOU,
SANDRA.

213
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:26,000
MR. POIROT
IS IT?

214
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:28,000
MONSIEUR RIDGEWAY.

215
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:30,000
MY ASSOCIATE,
CAPTAIN HASTINGS.

216
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:31,000
HOW DO
YOU DO?

217
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:33,000
PLEASE SIT
DOWN, GENTLEMEN.

218
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:37,000
THANK YOU.

219
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:39,000
I SUPPOSE YOU'VE
COME ABOUT MR. SHAW.

220
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:42,000
YOU HEARD WHAT
TOOK PLACE?

221
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:44,000
YES... BUT I'M SURE
IT WAS AN ACCIDENT.

222
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:46,000
WHY?

223
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:49,000
WELL, I MEAN, WHO'S GOING
TO KNOCK OFF OLD SHAW?

224
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:54,000
HE'S UTTERLY HARMLESS
AND DRY AS OLD BONES.

225
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:57,000
I UNDERSTAND THAT YOU WOULD
TRAVEL TO AMERICA

226
00:13:57,000 --> 00:13:59,000
IF MONSIEUR SHAW
WERE INDISPOSED.

227
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:01,000
YES, A BIT OF FUN, EH?

228
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:03,000
AND ON THE QUEEN MARY, TOO!

229
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:05,000
I'LL SAY.

230
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:06,000
Poirot:
YOU WOULD
LIKE TO GO?

231
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:08,000
OF COURSE I WOULD.

232
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:11,000
OH, BUT NOT
ENOUGH TO...

233
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:13,000
YOU DON'T THINK...

234
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:15,000
WHAT CAR DO YOU DRIVE,
MONSIEUR RIDGEWAY?

235
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:17,000
I DON'T.

236
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:18,000
I DID HAVE A CAR.

237
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:21,000
IT WAS A SINGER.

238
00:14:21,000 --> 00:14:22,000
THE COLOR?

239
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:24,000
RED.

240
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:27,000
BUT I HAVEN'T HAD IT FOR WEEKS.

241
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:28,000
YOU SEE, I SOLD IT.

242
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:30,000
I DIDN'T LIKE IT.

243
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:31,000
IT WAS THE IGNITION.

244
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:36,000
I COULD NEVER GET
THE DAMN THING TO START.

245
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:43,000
HE WAS LYING.

246
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:44,000
HE WAS NOT, PERHAPS

247
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:46,000
TELLING THE TRUTH
IN ENTIRETY.

248
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:48,000
THE SINGER'S GOT A
NEW IGNITION SYSTEM.

249
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:50,000
BEST ON THE ROAD.

250
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:52,000
AH, HASTINGS, ALWAYS
THE ENTHUSIAST.

251
00:14:52,000 --> 00:14:55,000
MR. POIROT?

252
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:59,000
MIGHT I... CAN I TALK TO YOU?

253
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:01,000
MY NAME IS
ESMEE DALGLEISH.

254
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:02,000
I'M ENGAGED
TO BE MARRIED

255
00:15:02,000 --> 00:15:04,000
TO PHILIP
RIDGEWAY.

256
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:05,000
I'D SAY HE'S
A LUCKY MAN.

257
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:07,000
THANK YOU.

258
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:11,000
AND YOU ARE ALSO THE SECRETARY
OF MONSIEUR VAVASOUR.

259
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:14,000
YES, THAT'S RIGHT.

260
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:16,000
HOW CAN I HELP
YOU, MADEMOISELLE?

261
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:20,000
MR. POIROT, MAY I SPEAK
TO YOU IN CONFIDENCE?

262
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:23,000
YOU HAVE MY ASSURANCE,
MADEMOISELLE.

263
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:25,000
I LOVE PHILIP VERY MUCH.

264
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:27,000
WE HOPE TO BE MARRIED
IN THE AUTUMN

265
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:31,000
BUT, IT'S JUST THESE
BONDS, MR. POIROT--

266
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:32,000
THE MONEY.

267
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:34,000
IT CONCERNS YOU.

268
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:35,000
YES.

269
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:38,000
BECAUSE IF MR. SHAW WERE
UNABLE TO GO TO AMERICA

270
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:40,000
PHILIP WOULD TAKE HIS PLACE

271
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:42,000
AND I'M AFRAID
FOR HIM, MR. POIROT.

272
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:43,000
Hastings:
YOU'RE AFRAID

273
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:46,000
SOMEONE MIGHT ATTACK HIM?

274
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:50,000
WELL... YES, THERE'S NO SAYING
WHAT SOME PEOPLE MIGHT DO

275
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:52,000
FOR SUCH A SUM OF MONEY.

276
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:54,000
MR. POIROT,
I KNOW YOU WILL DO

277
00:15:54,000 --> 00:15:56,000
EVERYTHING YOU CAN,
BUT I BEG OF YOU

278
00:15:56,000 --> 00:16:00,000
KEEP AN EYE ON PHILIP,
WHATEVER HAPPENS.

279
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:05,000
I'M FRIGHTENED HE'S GOING
TO COME TO HARM.

280
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:22,000
YOU'RE VERY PUNCTUAL,
MR. RIDGEWAY.

281
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:23,000
TIME FOR A PINT?

282
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:24,000
NO.

283
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:27,000
I HAVE TO GET BACK TO THE BANK.

284
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:28,000
OH, YES.

285
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:30,000
AND THE MONEY?

286
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:32,000
IT'S ON ITS WAY.

287
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:34,000
ANOTHER WEEK, THAT'S ALL.

288
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:36,000
ANOTHER WEEK?

289
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:38,000
TEN DAYS.

290
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:41,000
NO MORE.

291
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:42,000
I PROMISE YOU.

292
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:47,000
IT'S ALL ARRANGED.

293
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:15,000
AH, THANK YOU,
MRS. WINTER.

294
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:26,000
( choking sound )

295
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:36,000
THANK GOODNESS
YOU'RE BACK.

296
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:37,000
WHAT IS IT?

297
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:39,000
IT'S THE BANK--
THEY TELEPHONED.

298
00:17:39,000 --> 00:17:44,000
THEIR MR. SHAW,
HE'S BEEN POISONED!

299
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:48,000
Poirot:
GOOD EVENING.

300
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:50,000
WE WISH TO SEE MONSIEUR SHAW.

301
00:17:50,000 --> 00:17:54,000
AND YOU ARE...?

302
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:57,000
HERCULE POIROT.

303
00:17:57,000 --> 00:17:59,000
OH, YES. COME IN.

304
00:17:59,000 --> 00:18:04,000
THANK YOU.

305
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:08,000
Hastings:
HOW IS HE?

306
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:10,000
STILL VERY WEAK.

307
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:11,000
IT WAS STRYCHNINE.

308
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:12,000
STRYCHNINE?

309
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:14,000
IN HIS COFFEE.

310
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:16,000
MORE GUESTS, MR. SHAW.

311
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:18,000
JUST FIVE MINUTES,
THEN SLEEP.

312
00:18:18,000 --> 00:18:19,000
THANK YOU.

313
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:20,000
THANK YOU,
NURSE LONG.

314
00:18:20,000 --> 00:18:21,000
MR. POIROT...

315
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:24,000
NO, NO, NO,
MONSIEUR SHAW, PLEASE.

316
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:28,000
YOU MUST NOT TIRE YOURSELF.

317
00:18:28,000 --> 00:18:29,000
Vavasour:
IT WAS A CLOSE THING

318
00:18:29,000 --> 00:18:31,000
MR. POIROT.

319
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:33,000
ONE MORE MOUTHFUL AND...

320
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:35,000
I HAVE BEGUN AN INVESTIGATION.

321
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:36,000
Shaw:
IT COULD HAVE

322
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:37,000
BEEN... ANYONE.

323
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:40,000
McNeil:
YES, BUT AT
LEAST WE KNOW

324
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:41,000
WHO WAS THE LAST PERSON

325
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:44,000
IN MR. SHAW'S OFFICE
BEFORE THE COFFEE WAS DRUNK.

326
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:47,000
AND WHO WAS THAT,
MONSIEUR McNEIL?

327
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:52,000
THE SAME PERSON WHO WILL NOW
BE TAKING THE BONDS.

328
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:56,000
MR. RIDGEWAY.

329
00:18:56,000 --> 00:18:59,000
I THOUGHT YOU WERE GOING
TO TAKE ME OUT THIS EVENING.

330
00:18:59,000 --> 00:19:00,000
I WAS...

331
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:02,000
AND I WANT TO,
BUT I CAN'T.

332
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:04,000
I'M SORRY, OLD GIRL,
IT'S BUSINESS.

333
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:06,000
IT'S ALWAYS BUSINESS.

334
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:08,000
YOU SHOULD TALK
TO OLD VAVASOUR.

335
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:10,000
HE'S THE ONE
TO BLAME.

336
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:12,000
PHILIP, DO YOU
STILL LOVE ME?

337
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:16,000
WHAT?
OF COURSE I DO.

338
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:17,000
I'M WILD ABOUT YOU.

339
00:19:17,000 --> 00:19:19,000
I NEVER SEE
YOU ANYMORE.

340
00:19:19,000 --> 00:19:21,000
LOOK...

341
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:24,000
THINGS WILL
GET BETTER

342
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:28,000
ONCE I JUST...
TURN THE CORNER.

343
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:31,000
LOOK...

344
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:36,000
I'VE GOT TO FLY.

345
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:39,000
OH, DARLING, LOOK,
DAMN SILLY OF ME.

346
00:19:39,000 --> 00:19:42,000
I'VE LEFT MY WALLET
AT THE OFFICE.

347
00:19:42,000 --> 00:19:47,000
OH, PHILIP.

348
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:51,000
I SEEM TO KEEP
DOING THIS, DON'T I?

349
00:19:51,000 --> 00:19:53,000
I'VE GOT A COUPLE OF POUNDS.

350
00:19:53,000 --> 00:19:54,000
I'M SORRY, DARLING.

351
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:56,000
PHILIP, LOOK, IF
YOU'RE IN TROUBLE...

352
00:19:56,000 --> 00:19:58,000
OF COURSE I'M
NOT IN TROUBLE.

353
00:19:58,000 --> 00:19:59,000
...YOU CAN TELL ME.

354
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:02,000
EVERYTHING'S GOING
TO BE FINE.

355
00:20:02,000 --> 00:20:07,000
SEE YOU TOMORROW.

356
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:16,000
Vavasour:
THE KEYS, MR. McNEIL.

357
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:19,000
YOU KNOW WHAT TO DO IN
NEW YORK, MR. RIDGEWAY?

358
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:20,000
YES, SIR.

359
00:20:20,000 --> 00:20:21,000
GOOD.

360
00:20:21,000 --> 00:20:22,000
ONE FOR YOU, MR. RIDGEWAY.

361
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:26,000
MR. McNEIL, YOU ARE RESPONSIBLE
FOR DELIVERING THAT

362
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:28,000
TO MR. SHAW
AT HIS HOME.

363
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:30,000
VERY GOOD, SIR.

364
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:33,000
AND ONE FOR ME.

365
00:20:33,000 --> 00:20:36,000
IS MR. SHAW STILL
NOT BETTER, SIR?

366
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:39,000
I'M AFRAID HE'LL BE IN BED
FOR AT LEAST TWO WEEKS.

367
00:20:39,000 --> 00:20:41,000
I'D BE GLAD

368
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:43,000
TO MAKE THE
JOURNEY, SIR.

369
00:20:43,000 --> 00:20:44,000
THANK YOU, MR. McNEIL

370
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:47,000
BUT THERE'S BUSINESS
TO BE DONE IN NEW YORK

371
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:49,000
WHICH IN MR. SHAW'S ABSENCE

372
00:20:49,000 --> 00:20:53,000
ONLY MR. RIDGEWAY
CAN HANDLE.

373
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:54,000
ONLY TEN DAYS,
OLD GIRL--

374
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:56,000
MAYBE THE FASTEST
CROSSING EVER.

375
00:20:56,000 --> 00:20:58,000
I'LL TAKE
NO CHANCES

376
00:20:58,000 --> 00:21:00,000
WITH YOUR
FIANCE'S SAFETY,
MISS DALGLEISH.

377
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:03,000
AFTER WHAT HAS
HAPPENED TO MR. SHAW

378
00:21:03,000 --> 00:21:06,000
I HAVE ASKED MR. POIROT
TO ACCOMPANY THE BONDS.

379
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:09,000
HE'S LETTING ME
KNOW LATER TODAY.

380
00:21:09,000 --> 00:21:11,000
WITH DUE RESPECT,
I CAN'T QUITE SEE

381
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:16,000
WHAT'S TO BE GAINED
BY EMPLOYING A BELGIAN.

382
00:21:19,000 --> 00:21:23,000
Esmee:
IT'S JUST THESE BONDS,
MR. POIROT-- THE MONEY.

383
00:21:23,000 --> 00:21:25,000
I LOVE PHILIP VERY MUCH.

384
00:21:25,000 --> 00:21:29,000
I KNOW YOU WILL DO
EVERYTHING YOU CAN

385
00:21:29,000 --> 00:21:34,000
BUT PLEASE, I BEG OF YOU,
KEEP AN EYE ON PHILIP.

386
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:36,000
Woman:
COME ON,
JONATHAN.

387
00:21:36,000 --> 00:21:41,000
IT'S TIME WE
WERE HOME.

388
00:21:49,000 --> 00:21:51,000
Miss Lemon:
I'VE PUT IN
YOUR BLUE TIE

389
00:21:51,000 --> 00:21:53,000
AND THE MAUVE
SILK WAISTCOAT.

390
00:21:53,000 --> 00:21:56,000
Poirot:
AND I SHALL TAKE
ALSO THE BROWN SUIT

391
00:21:56,000 --> 00:21:58,000
AND THE TWO
WAISTCOATS
THAT COORDINATE.

392
00:21:58,000 --> 00:22:00,000
YOU CAN'T TAKE

393
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:04,000
YOUR ENTIRE WARDROBE,
MR. POIROT.

394
00:22:04,000 --> 00:22:05,000
POIROT.

395
00:22:05,000 --> 00:22:06,000
AH, HASTINGS,
ENFIN.

396
00:22:06,000 --> 00:22:09,000
YOU MUST BEGIN AT
ONCE THE PACKING.

397
00:22:09,000 --> 00:22:10,000
WE'RE GOING?

398
00:22:10,000 --> 00:22:11,000
ON THE
QUEEN MARY.

399
00:22:11,000 --> 00:22:12,000
YOU AND ME?

400
00:22:12,000 --> 00:22:14,000
YES, WE TRAVEL WITH THE BONDS.

401
00:22:14,000 --> 00:22:15,000
I HAD THIS CONFIRMED

402
00:22:15,000 --> 00:22:16,000
WITH MONSIEUR
VAVASOUR TODAY.

403
00:22:16,000 --> 00:22:18,000
THAT'S WONDERFUL!

404
00:22:18,000 --> 00:22:21,000
WHAT ON EARTH
MADE YOU CHANGE
YOUR MIND?

405
00:22:21,000 --> 00:22:23,000
I CANNOT REFUSE A LADY.

406
00:22:23,000 --> 00:22:24,000
ESPECIALLY IF SHE'S A QUEEN.

407
00:22:24,000 --> 00:22:27,000
I PROMISE YOU
WON'T HAVE
SEASICKNESS.

408
00:22:27,000 --> 00:22:28,000
SO YOU SAY,
MON AMI.

409
00:22:28,000 --> 00:22:33,000
BUT I TAKE
THE PRECAUTIONS
ALL THE SAME.

410
00:23:25,000 --> 00:23:30,000
ONE MILLION DOLLARS
IN LIBERTY BONDS.

411
00:23:47,000 --> 00:23:50,000
Newsreel announcer:
New York-bound at last.

412
00:23:50,000 --> 00:23:53,000
The Queen Mary
on her maiden voyage.

413
00:23:53,000 --> 00:23:56,000
Tens of thousands have
poured into Southampton

414
00:23:56,000 --> 00:24:00,000
to glimpse the world's newest
and greatest liner.

415
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:04,000
But what of the privileged few
who will sail aboard her?

416
00:24:04,000 --> 00:24:07,000
On or two will hardly
remember the occasion

417
00:24:07,000 --> 00:24:09,000
whilst others are determined

418
00:24:09,000 --> 00:24:13,000
that this will be one trip
that they won't forget.

419
00:24:13,000 --> 00:24:17,000
And here's a familiar face--
Europe's most famous detective

420
00:24:17,000 --> 00:24:20,000
Hercule Poirot, hot on the track
of a well-deserved break

421
00:24:20,000 --> 00:24:23,000
and looking forward
to a life on the ocean wave.

422
00:24:23,000 --> 00:24:25,000
Another "case"
for Monsieur Poirot.

423
00:24:25,000 --> 00:24:29,000
There are over 2,000 cases
being loaded on board

424
00:24:29,000 --> 00:24:31,000
and it's certainly
an arresting site

425
00:24:31,000 --> 00:24:36,000
as the sailing hour arrives,
and the Queen Mary puts to sea.

426
00:24:38,000 --> 00:24:42,000
Our camera takes to the air
as Britain's newest liner

427
00:24:42,000 --> 00:24:44,000
leaves the sanctuary
of home waters

428
00:24:44,000 --> 00:24:48,000
and heads into the Atlantic
Ocean for the first time.

429
00:24:48,000 --> 00:24:50,000
But will she steal
that blue ribbon?

430
00:24:50,000 --> 00:24:53,000
It's currently held
by the Normandy

431
00:24:53,000 --> 00:24:58,000
with a crossing time
of just four days.

432
00:25:08,000 --> 00:25:09,000
BONJOUR.

433
00:25:09,000 --> 00:25:14,000
MORNING.

434
00:25:22,000 --> 00:25:25,000
GOOD MORNING, MR. POIROT.

435
00:25:25,000 --> 00:25:30,000
BONJOUR, MADEMOISELLE.

436
00:25:31,000 --> 00:25:36,000
( knocks )

437
00:25:52,000 --> 00:25:53,000

BONJOUR, HASTINGS.

438
00:25:53,000 --> 00:25:57,000
COMMENT CA VA?

439
00:25:57,000 --> 00:25:59,000
I'M TERRIBLE.

440
00:25:59,000 --> 00:26:02,000
I TELL YOU, POIROT,
IT'S NOT SEASICKNESS.

441
00:26:02,000 --> 00:26:05,000
I'M NEVER SEASICK.

442
00:26:05,000 --> 00:26:07,000
MUST HAVE BEEN
THAT OYSTER LAST NIGHT.

443
00:26:07,000 --> 00:26:10,000
IF YOU WISH, I HAVE SOME PILLS.

444
00:26:10,000 --> 00:26:11,000
THANK YOU,
POIROT.

445
00:26:11,000 --> 00:26:16,000
I'LL BE PERFECTLY ALL RIGHT.

446
00:26:17,000 --> 00:26:20,000
OH, I SAY, POIROT.

447
00:26:20,000 --> 00:26:22,000
THERE'S A YOUNG LADY
IN THE CABIN NEXT DOOR.

448
00:26:22,000 --> 00:26:24,000
YES, WE JUST MET.

449
00:26:24,000 --> 00:26:26,000
MISS BROOKS-- MIRANDA.

450
00:26:26,000 --> 00:26:30,000
WE WERE SUPPOSED
TO GO SWIMMING TOGETHER.

451
00:26:30,000 --> 00:26:34,000
IF YOU SEE HER AGAIN,
COULD YOU TELL HER I'M...

452
00:26:34,000 --> 00:26:39,000
THE BAD OYSTER, NON?

453
00:27:01,000 --> 00:27:06,000
Ridgeway:
YES, BRING IT IN.

454
00:27:12,000 --> 00:27:15,000
OH, GOOD MORNING.

455
00:27:15,000 --> 00:27:18,000
BONJOUR, MONSIEUR
RIDGEWAY.

456
00:27:18,000 --> 00:27:20,000
I THOUGHT YOU
WERE THE STEWARD.

457
00:27:20,000 --> 00:27:22,000
NO.

458
00:27:22,000 --> 00:27:24,000
YOU HAVE NOT YET HAD
THE BREAKFAST?

459
00:27:24,000 --> 00:27:26,000
NO...

460
00:27:26,000 --> 00:27:31,000
ACTUALLY, I HAD A BIT
OF A NIGHT OF IT.

461
00:27:32,000 --> 00:27:34,000
OUI.

462
00:27:34,000 --> 00:27:35,000
AND THE PORTMANTEAU?

463
00:27:35,000 --> 00:27:37,000
OH.

464
00:27:37,000 --> 00:27:40,000
THE KEY'S PERFECTLY
SAFE, MR. POIROT.

465
00:27:40,000 --> 00:27:41,000
DON'T WORRY.

466
00:27:41,000 --> 00:27:43,000
I KEEP THE KEY
IN MY POCKET

467
00:27:43,000 --> 00:27:44,000
AND LOCK
THE CABIN DOOR

468
00:27:44,000 --> 00:27:48,000
EACH TIME
I GO OUT.

469
00:27:48,000 --> 00:27:51,000
IF YOU SEE THE STEWARD,
ASK HIM TO GET A MOVE ON.

470
00:27:51,000 --> 00:27:56,000
I'M FAMISHED.

471
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:01,000
WELL, HELLO
AGAIN.

472
00:28:01,000 --> 00:28:03,000
AH, MADEMOISELLE.

473
00:28:03,000 --> 00:28:05,000
CAPTAIN HASTINGS
REGRETS THAT HE IS UNABLE

474
00:28:05,000 --> 00:28:07,000
TO SWIM WITH YOU TODAY.

475
00:28:07,000 --> 00:28:08,000
OH, THAT'S OKAY.

476
00:28:08,000 --> 00:28:11,000
I WAS FEELING
PRETTY TERRIBLE MYSELF.

477
00:28:11,000 --> 00:28:13,000
I WAS DANCING UNTIL 3:00.

478
00:28:13,000 --> 00:28:16,000
YET YOU ARE TRAVELING ALONE,
MADEMOISELLE BROOKS?

479
00:28:16,000 --> 00:28:19,000
YOU'RE NEVER ALONE
ON A SHIP, MR. POIROT.

480
00:28:19,000 --> 00:28:24,000
I'LL SEE YOU.

481
00:28:24,000 --> 00:28:28,000
MADEMOISELLE, PARDON BUT...

482
00:28:28,000 --> 00:28:33,000
WHAT IS THE TIME?

483
00:28:33,000 --> 00:28:37,000
IT'S JUST 9:30.

484
00:28:37,000 --> 00:28:42,000
THANK YOU.

485
00:29:34,000 --> 00:29:36,000
AH, MR. POIROT.

486
00:29:36,000 --> 00:29:37,000
GOOD MORNING.

487
00:29:37,000 --> 00:29:40,000
BONJOUR.

488
00:29:40,000 --> 00:29:42,000
THE CAPTAIN WON'T BE
AT HIS TABLE.

489
00:29:42,000 --> 00:29:43,000
THERE IS A PROBLEM?

490
00:29:43,000 --> 00:29:46,000
THERE'S BEEN
A PATCH OF FOG
FORECAST, SIR.

491
00:29:46,000 --> 00:29:49,000
THE CAPTAIN WILL HAVE
TO REMAIN ON THE BRIDGE.

492
00:29:49,000 --> 00:29:53,000
AH, WELL, PLEASE TO CONVEY
MY REGRETS TO THE CAPTAIN.

493
00:29:53,000 --> 00:29:55,000
WE MAY LOSE THE BLUE RIBBON.

494
00:29:55,000 --> 00:29:57,000
THERE'S ALWAYS
NEXT TIME.

495
00:29:57,000 --> 00:29:58,000
OUI.

496
00:29:58,000 --> 00:29:59,000
GOOD MORNING, SIR.

497
00:29:59,000 --> 00:30:04,000
GOOD MORNING.

498
00:30:19,000 --> 00:30:24,000
( soft music )

499
00:30:32,000 --> 00:30:35,000
JUST A LITTLE FISH
FOR ME, PLEASE

500
00:30:35,000 --> 00:30:40,000
POACHED WITH DRY TOAST.

501
00:30:40,000 --> 00:30:41,000

MERCI BEAUCOUP.

502
00:30:41,000 --> 00:30:43,000
MAIS C'EST
INCROYABLE.

503
00:30:43,000 --> 00:30:48,000
THIS SHIP THAT IS NOT A SHIP,
IT IS, HOW YOU SAY... A MARVEL.

504
00:30:48,000 --> 00:30:49,000
YES, POIROT.

505
00:30:49,000 --> 00:30:50,000
AH, BUT OF COURSE

506
00:30:50,000 --> 00:30:52,000
MY POOR HASTINGS STILL HAS...

507
00:30:52,000 --> 00:30:55,000
FOOD POISONING.

508
00:30:55,000 --> 00:30:57,000
EVENING, RIDGEWAY.

509
00:30:57,000 --> 00:30:59,000
CAN WE COUNT
YOU IN TONIGHT?

510
00:30:59,000 --> 00:31:00,000
I'LL BE THERE.

511
00:31:00,000 --> 00:31:05,000
SEE IF YOU CAN WIN BACK
SOME OF THAT MONEY, EH?

512
00:31:05,000 --> 00:31:06,000
YOU PLAY THE CARDS?

513
00:31:06,000 --> 00:31:10,000
YES... IT PASSES THE TIME...
AND IT'S ALL VERY FRIENDLY.

514
00:31:10,000 --> 00:31:13,000
WE JUST
PLAY FOR A
FEW POUNDS.

515
00:31:13,000 --> 00:31:17,000
AH, MERCI.

516
00:31:17,000 --> 00:31:19,000
AH! LES CERVELLES
AU BEURRE!

517
00:31:19,000 --> 00:31:21,000
OH, WHAT'S THAT?

518
00:31:21,000 --> 00:31:26,000
IT IS THE BRAINS OF THE CALF
FRIED IN BUTTER.

519
00:31:26,000 --> 00:31:31,000
I THINK PERHAPS I'LL GO
AND HAVE ANOTHER LIE DOWN.

520
00:31:36,000 --> 00:31:39,000
( horn blows )

521
00:31:39,000 --> 00:31:44,000
( laughter )

522
00:32:00,000 --> 00:32:03,000
QUEEN'S HIGH, DAMN IT.

523
00:32:03,000 --> 00:32:06,000
WELL...

524
00:32:06,000 --> 00:32:11,000
I'M AFRAID YOU'RE
BLOWN, RIDGEWAY.

525
00:32:12,000 --> 00:32:16,000
YES.

526
00:32:16,000 --> 00:32:21,000
I'M SURE YOU'LL ACCEPT AN I.O.U.

527
00:33:03,000 --> 00:33:08,000
( splash )

528
00:33:14,000 --> 00:33:15,000
OH, MISS BROOKS!

529
00:33:15,000 --> 00:33:16,000
MIRANDA.

530
00:33:16,000 --> 00:33:19,000
WHY, CAPTAIN HASTINGS,
CAN'T YOU SLEEP?

531
00:33:19,000 --> 00:33:20,000
NO, I COULDN'T.

532
00:33:20,000 --> 00:33:22,000
I THOUGHT I HEARD...

533
00:33:22,000 --> 00:33:25,000
SOMEONE DIDN'T GO OVERBOARD
JUST NOW, DID THEY?

534
00:33:25,000 --> 00:33:26,000
ONLY THE ORCHESTRA.

535
00:33:26,000 --> 00:33:29,000
THEY'VE BEEN GOING
OVERBOARD ALL NIGHT.

536
00:33:29,000 --> 00:33:32,000
YES! I'M SORRY
I COULDN'T JOIN YOU.

537
00:33:32,000 --> 00:33:34,000
I'M SORRY YOU COULDN'T MAKE IT.

538
00:33:34,000 --> 00:33:38,000
STILL, WE'LL BE IN NEW YORK
IN A FEW HOURS.

539
00:33:38,000 --> 00:33:39,000
PERHAPS, WE COULD...

540
00:33:39,000 --> 00:33:43,000
YES, WELL,
MAYBE WE'LL MEET AGAIN.

541
00:33:43,000 --> 00:33:46,000

WELL... YES.

542
00:33:46,000 --> 00:33:48,000
MISS BROOKS?

543
00:33:48,000 --> 00:33:53,000
GOOD NIGHT,
CAPTAIN HASTINGS.

544
00:34:06,000 --> 00:34:11,000
RIDGEWAY?

545
00:34:27,000 --> 00:34:28,000
CAPTAIN HASTINGS.

546
00:34:28,000 --> 00:34:33,000
RIDGEWAY! THE BONDS!

547
00:34:42,000 --> 00:34:46,000
WAIT HERE, PLEASE.

548
00:34:46,000 --> 00:34:49,000
IS IT REALLY TRUE,
THEY'VE GONE?

549
00:34:49,000 --> 00:34:51,000
YES, SIR, I'M AFRAID SO.

550
00:34:51,000 --> 00:34:53,000
BUT THEY'RE AN HOUR
FROM NEW YORK.

551
00:34:53,000 --> 00:34:56,000
THEY MUST STILL BE
ON THE SHIP.

552
00:34:56,000 --> 00:34:59,000
I'VE CABLED THEM TO START
A PERSON-TO-PERSON SEARCH

553
00:34:59,000 --> 00:35:02,000
BUT IT WOULD BE EASIER
IF I WERE THERE.

554
00:35:02,000 --> 00:35:03,000
THEY MUST BE FOUND.

555
00:35:03,000 --> 00:35:07,000
IF THEY'RE SOLD, IT COULD
BRING DOWN THE ENTIRE BANK.

556
00:35:07,000 --> 00:35:09,000
I'M AWARE OF THAT, SIR

557
00:35:09,000 --> 00:35:11,000
WHICH IS WHY I MUST ASK
ONE QUESTION.

558
00:35:11,000 --> 00:35:13,000
OF COURSE, ANYTHING.

559
00:35:13,000 --> 00:35:18,000
DO YOU STILL HAVE
THE KEY I GAVE YOU?

560
00:35:19,000 --> 00:35:22,000
IT HASN'T LEFT MY SIGHT.

561
00:35:22,000 --> 00:35:25,000
Newsreel announcer:
Britain's greatest liner

562
00:35:25,000 --> 00:35:29,000
steams into New York at the end
of her first Atlantic crossing

563
00:35:29,000 --> 00:35:31,000
after fog delayed her
for 11 hours.

564
00:35:31,000 --> 00:35:34,000
Even so, New York gave
a frenzied welcome

565
00:35:34,000 --> 00:35:36,000
to Britain's queen of the sea.

566
00:35:36,000 --> 00:35:40,000
The crossing was completed in
four days, 12 hours, 24 minutes

567
00:35:40,000 --> 00:35:43,000
at an average speed of 29 knots.

568
00:35:43,000 --> 00:35:45,000
And just listen
to that roar of welcome.

569
00:35:45,000 --> 00:35:50,000
( cheering )

570
00:35:51,000 --> 00:35:54,000
Ridgeway:
I SWEAR TO HEAVEN,
MR. POIROT

571
00:35:54,000 --> 00:35:56,000
I HAD THE KEY
ALL THE TIME.

572
00:35:56,000 --> 00:35:59,000
AND WHERE WERE YOU
ALL NIGHT, RIDGEWAY?

573
00:35:59,000 --> 00:36:00,000
I WAS PLAYING CARDS.

574
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:03,000
I KNOW I SHOULD
HAVE BEEN HERE, BUT...

575
00:36:03,000 --> 00:36:05,000
I SUPPOSE IT'S A
WEAKNESS OF MINE.

576
00:36:05,000 --> 00:36:06,000
GAMBLING?

577
00:36:06,000 --> 00:36:08,000
HOW MUCH DID YOU LOSE?

578
00:36:08,000 --> 00:36:09,000
ABOUT 100 POUNDS

579
00:36:09,000 --> 00:36:11,000
AND THE SAME
THE NIGHT BEFORE.

580
00:36:11,000 --> 00:36:14,000
THIS DOESN'T LOOK
TOO GOOD FOR ME

581
00:36:14,000 --> 00:36:15,000
DOES IT?

582
00:36:15,000 --> 00:36:17,000
LEAVE US,
MONSIEUR
RIDGEWAY.

583
00:36:17,000 --> 00:36:22,000
WE SHALL SPEAK AGAIN.

584
00:36:22,000 --> 00:36:27,000
I'LL GO AND MAKE MY REPORT
TO THE CAPTAIN.

585
00:36:27,000 --> 00:36:30,000
I SAY, LOOK
AT THIS, POIROT.

586
00:36:30,000 --> 00:36:32,000
IT'S CUT AND SCRATCHED
AT THE BACK HERE.

587
00:36:32,000 --> 00:36:35,000
OUI, THIS I HAVE
EXAMINED ALREADY.

588
00:36:35,000 --> 00:36:37,000
SOMEONE TRIED
TO FORCE IT.

589
00:36:37,000 --> 00:36:38,000
PRECISEMENT.

590
00:36:38,000 --> 00:36:41,000
BUT THEN THEY MANAGED
TO UNLOCK IT ANYWAY.

591
00:36:41,000 --> 00:36:44,000
HMM... CURIOUS.

592
00:36:44,000 --> 00:36:46,000
IT IS VERY CURIOUS.

593
00:36:46,000 --> 00:36:49,000
THEY WASTE MUCH TIME
TRYING TO PRY IT OPEN

594
00:36:49,000 --> 00:36:50,000
AND THEN SAPRISTI

595
00:36:50,000 --> 00:36:53,000
THEY FIND EY HAVE
THE KEY ALL THE TIME.

596
00:36:53,000 --> 00:36:56,000
UNLESS THEY WANTED
TO MAKE IT LOOK AS
IF IT WAS FORCED.

597
00:36:56,000 --> 00:36:58,000
OUI, C'EST POSSIBLE.

598
00:36:58,000 --> 00:37:01,000
BUT THEN IT MUST
HAVE BEEN RIDGEWAY.

599
00:37:01,000 --> 00:37:02,000
NOBODY ELSE HAD A KEY.

600
00:37:02,000 --> 00:37:04,000
YOU ARE
DISAPPOINTED?

601
00:37:04,000 --> 00:37:07,000
HE'S A BIT OF AN ASS,
BUT I DIDN'T THINK HE'D...

602
00:37:07,000 --> 00:37:10,000
NO, NEITHER DID I, MON AMI.

603
00:37:10,000 --> 00:37:13,000
( cheering outside )

604
00:37:13,000 --> 00:37:15,000
WE HAVE TO
FIND THEM, McNEIL.

605
00:37:15,000 --> 00:37:17,000
YES, SIR.

606
00:37:17,000 --> 00:37:20,000
OR THE PERSON
WHO STOLE THEM, SIR.

607
00:37:20,000 --> 00:37:21,000

QUITE.

608
00:37:21,000 --> 00:37:22,000
MR. SHAW HAD HIS KEY?

609
00:37:22,000 --> 00:37:23,000
YES, SIR.

610
00:37:23,000 --> 00:37:24,000
YES, OF COURSE.

611
00:37:24,000 --> 00:37:26,000
DO YOU HAVE YOURS, SIR?

612
00:37:26,000 --> 00:37:28,000
OF COURSE I HAVE.

613
00:37:28,000 --> 00:37:30,000
MAY I SEE IT,
PLEASE, SIR?

614
00:37:30,000 --> 00:37:34,000
REALLY, McNEIL!

615
00:37:34,000 --> 00:37:36,000
( horn blows )

616
00:37:36,000 --> 00:37:38,000
Hastings:
SO I CAME OUT HERE

617
00:37:38,000 --> 00:37:43,000
WENT OVER TO
THE RAIL HERE.

618
00:37:45,000 --> 00:37:47,000
THEN I HEARD A SPLASH

619
00:37:47,000 --> 00:37:52,000
WHICH SEEMED TO COME
FROM OVER THERE.

620
00:37:54,000 --> 00:37:55,000
NOW, THIS IS WHERE

621
00:37:55,000 --> 00:37:57,000
I MET MIRANDA.

622
00:37:57,000 --> 00:37:58,000
MADEMOISELLE
BROOKS?

623
00:37:58,000 --> 00:38:02,000
YES, SHE CAME
FROM OVER THERE.

624
00:38:02,000 --> 00:38:04,000
NOW, THE CABIN
OF MONSIEUR RIDGEWAY

625
00:38:04,000 --> 00:38:07,000
IT LOOKS OUT ONTO
THIS DECK, DOES IT NOT?

626
00:38:07,000 --> 00:38:08,000
YES... YES, IT DOES.

627
00:38:08,000 --> 00:38:11,000
BUT SHE WAS
CARRYING NOTHING?

628
00:38:11,000 --> 00:38:12,000
NO.

629
00:38:12,000 --> 00:38:13,000
IF SHE HAD TAKEN THEM

630
00:38:13,000 --> 00:38:16,000
SHE COULD HAVE
THROWN THEM OVERBOARD

631
00:38:16,000 --> 00:38:20,000
AND THEN THEY COULD HAVE
DRIFTED INTO NEW YORK.

632
00:38:20,000 --> 00:38:23,000
AND THEN... PERHAPS
THEY GREW THE LITTLE FINS

633
00:38:23,000 --> 00:38:26,000
AND SWAM ASHORE?

634
00:38:26,000 --> 00:38:31,000
YES... IT IS
A STUPID IDEA.

635
00:38:32,000 --> 00:38:37,000
AU CONTRAIRE, MY DEAR HASTINGS,
YOU ARE AS PERCEPTIVE AS EVER.

636
00:38:48,000 --> 00:38:51,000
WAIT A MINUTE.

637
00:38:51,000 --> 00:38:55,000
IT WAS HERE.

638
00:38:55,000 --> 00:38:59,000
MR. VAVASOUR, DO YOU REALIZE
HOW SERIOUS THIS MATTER IS?

639
00:38:59,000 --> 00:39:00,000
OF COURSE I DO.

640
00:39:00,000 --> 00:39:02,000
THIS IS A MATTER FOR THE POLICE.

641
00:39:02,000 --> 00:39:03,000
POLICE?

642
00:39:03,000 --> 00:39:05,000
YES, SIR.

643
00:39:05,000 --> 00:39:07,000
YOUR KEY,
YOUR SECRETARY'S FIANCEE

644
00:39:07,000 --> 00:39:10,000
AND YOUR IDEA TO SEND
THE BONDS IN THE FIRST PLACE.

645
00:39:10,000 --> 00:39:13,000
McNEILYOU WORK FOR ME!

646
00:39:13,000 --> 00:39:15,000
I THINK YOU BETTER
COME WITH ME, SIR

647
00:39:15,000 --> 00:39:20,000
DOWN TO THE YARD.

648
00:39:20,000 --> 00:39:21,000
AH, MR. POIROT--

649
00:39:21,000 --> 00:39:23,000
HAVE YOU MADE
ANY PROGRESS, SIR?

650
00:39:23,000 --> 00:39:25,000
WE MAKE GREAT STEPS.

651
00:39:25,000 --> 00:39:27,000
I WISH I COULD
SAY THE SAME.

652
00:39:27,000 --> 00:39:28,000
THIS IS A
CUSTOMS OFFICER.

653
00:39:28,000 --> 00:39:30,000
NAME'S TOM
FRANKLIN, SIR.

654
00:39:30,000 --> 00:39:32,000
I'M HONORED TO
SHAKE THE HAND

655
00:39:32,000 --> 00:39:34,000
OF THE FAMOUS
HERCULE POIROT.

656
00:39:34,000 --> 00:39:35,000
THANK YOU.

657
00:39:35,000 --> 00:39:38,000
YOU HAVE BEGUN THE SEARCH,
MONSIEUR?

658
00:39:38,000 --> 00:39:39,000
YES, SIR.

659
00:39:39,000 --> 00:39:41,000
A BENT DIME COULDN'T
GET PAST MY MEN

660
00:39:41,000 --> 00:39:43,000
BUT SO FAR, NOTHING.

661
00:39:43,000 --> 00:39:46,000
HAS MISS BROOKS GONE ASHORE?
BLONDE AMERICAN GIRL

662
00:39:46,000 --> 00:39:47,000
VERY BEAUTIFUL.

663
00:39:47,000 --> 00:39:51,000
SIR, THERE WERE OVER
1,000 PASSENGERS ON BOARD.

664
00:39:51,000 --> 00:39:52,000
YOU'RE TOO LATE.

665
00:39:52,000 --> 00:39:55,000
YOUR BONDS WILL NOT
BE FOUND ON THE PASSENGERS

666
00:39:55,000 --> 00:39:57,000
AND THEY ARE NOT ON THE SHIP.

667
00:39:57,000 --> 00:39:58,000
THAT'S IMPOSSIBLE, SIR.

668
00:39:58,000 --> 00:40:01,000
THEY CAN'T HAVE
GOT OFF THE SHIP.

669
00:40:01,000 --> 00:40:03,000
I ASSURE YOU THAT IS THE CASE.

670
00:40:03,000 --> 00:40:04,000
THERE IS NOTHING HERE.

671
00:40:04,000 --> 00:40:07,000
HASTINGS, WE
MUST RETURN TO
LONDON AT ONCE.

672
00:40:07,000 --> 00:40:08,000
AND MR. RIDGEWAY?

673
00:40:08,000 --> 00:40:10,000
HE WILL RETURN
WITH US.

674
00:40:10,000 --> 00:40:12,000
WHAT ABOUT THE SEARCH,
MR. POIROT?

675
00:40:12,000 --> 00:40:14,000
YOUR MR. McNEIL WAS
PRETTY INSISTENT.

676
00:40:14,000 --> 00:40:19,000
I ASSURE YOU, OFFICER, MONSIEUR
McNEIL DOES NOT BELONG TO ME.

677
00:40:21,000 --> 00:40:24,000
MR. McNEIL,
WHERE IS MR. VAVASOUR?

678
00:40:24,000 --> 00:40:26,000
HE IS AT THE POLICE STATION.

679
00:40:26,000 --> 00:40:28,000
THE POLICE?-- WHY?

680
00:40:28,000 --> 00:40:32,000
THAT IS CONFIDENTIAL
INFORMATION, MISS DALGLEISH.

681
00:40:32,000 --> 00:40:34,000
HE IS THE GENERAL MANAGER
OF THIS BANK

682
00:40:34,000 --> 00:40:35,000
AND I AM HIS SECRETARY.

683
00:40:35,000 --> 00:40:37,000
THAT MAKES NO DIFFERENCE.

684
00:40:37,000 --> 00:40:38,000
I HAVE A RIGHT TO KNOW.

685
00:40:38,000 --> 00:40:40,000
THIS IS RIDICULOUS!

686
00:40:40,000 --> 00:40:42,000
BUT LET ME REMIND YOU,
MR. McNEIL

687
00:40:42,000 --> 00:40:44,000
IN A FEW DAYS
MR. POIROT WILL BE BACK.

688
00:40:44,000 --> 00:40:46,000
I DON'T SEE HOW

689
00:40:46,000 --> 00:40:51,000
HE CAN HELP.

690
00:40:54,000 --> 00:40:56,000
Newsreel announcer:
And home again.

691
00:40:56,000 --> 00:40:59,000
The Queen Mary returns
to home waters.

692
00:40:59,000 --> 00:41:03,000
As we circle round, another
member of the line passes--

693
00:41:03,000 --> 00:41:05,000
the Berengaria, outward bound

694
00:41:05,000 --> 00:41:08,000
two great vessels
passing at sea.

695
00:41:08,000 --> 00:41:12,000
And now the Queen Mary heads
into Southampton water

696
00:41:12,000 --> 00:41:14,000
and prepares to berth.

697
00:41:14,000 --> 00:41:18,000
Many happy returns
to your home waters.

698
00:41:18,000 --> 00:41:23,000
( cheering, horns blowing )

699
00:41:48,000 --> 00:41:53,000
GOOD TO BE HOME,
EH, POIROT?

700
00:41:53,000 --> 00:41:58,000
OH, LOOK, THERE'S
YOUR FIANCEE.

701
00:42:04,000 --> 00:42:05,000
OFFICERS.

702
00:42:05,000 --> 00:42:07,000
YES, SIR.

703
00:42:07,000 --> 00:42:08,000
MR. POIROT.

704
00:42:08,000 --> 00:42:10,000
I WANT YOU TO
ARREST THIS MAN

705
00:42:10,000 --> 00:42:12,000
FOR THE THEFT OF
ONE MILLION DOLLARS

706
00:42:12,000 --> 00:42:13,000
IN LIBERTY BONDS.

707
00:42:13,000 --> 00:42:14,000
WHAT?

708
00:42:14,000 --> 00:42:16,000
I SAY,
POIROT!

709
00:42:16,000 --> 00:42:17,000
IF YOU
SAY SO, SIR.

710
00:42:17,000 --> 00:42:22,000
COME ON, YOU.

711
00:42:22,000 --> 00:42:27,000
HOW COULD YOU?

712
00:42:31,000 --> 00:42:34,000
IT LOOKED SUCH A
BEAUTIFUL SHIP, MR. POIROT.

713
00:42:34,000 --> 00:42:37,000
IT WAS AN EXPERIENCE
MOST REMARKABLE,
MISS LEMON.

714
00:42:37,000 --> 00:42:41,000
I'M ONLY SORRY IT WASN'T
ALL MORE SUCCESSFUL.

715
00:42:41,000 --> 00:42:43,000
BUT IT WAS
A GREAT SUCCESS.

716
00:42:43,000 --> 00:42:46,000
NOT ONCE DID I SUCCUMB
TO THE MAL DE MER.

717
00:42:46,000 --> 00:42:47,000
POIROT.

718
00:42:47,000 --> 00:42:49,000
AH, HASTINGS,
YOU ARE READY.

719
00:42:49,000 --> 00:42:52,000
WE HAVE PLAYED THE GAMES
LONG ENOUGH.

720
00:42:52,000 --> 00:42:57,000
IT IS NOW TIME
TO SETTLE THE SCORES.

721
00:43:11,000 --> 00:43:12,000
MR. POIROT!

722
00:43:12,000 --> 00:43:14,000
THIS IS MONSTROUS.

723
00:43:14,000 --> 00:43:16,000
I DO NOT KNOW
WHAT HAPPENED TO MY KEY.

724
00:43:16,000 --> 00:43:19,000
WHEN DID YOU NOTICE
IT HAD GONE, MONSIEUR?

725
00:43:19,000 --> 00:43:21,000
ONLY WHEN McNEIL
ASKED FOR IT.

726
00:43:21,000 --> 00:43:24,000
WHO THEN HAD ACCESS
TO YOUR OFFICE?

727
00:43:24,000 --> 00:43:26,000
MYSELF,
MY SECRETARY...

728
00:43:26,000 --> 00:43:28,000
ONE MORE QUESTION,
MONSIEUR.

729
00:43:28,000 --> 00:43:30,000
BEFORE THE DEPARTURE
OF THE QUEEN MARY

730
00:43:30,000 --> 00:43:33,000
WHO PUT THE BONDS
INTO THE PORTMANTEAU?

731
00:43:33,000 --> 00:43:34,000
I DID, WHY?

732
00:43:34,000 --> 00:43:36,000
IT IS AS I THOUGHT,
MONSIEUR

733
00:43:36,000 --> 00:43:39,000
AND IT TELLS ME ALL
THAT I NEED TO KNOW.

734
00:43:39,000 --> 00:43:42,000
THANK YOU.

735
00:43:42,000 --> 00:43:45,000
MR. POIROT!

736
00:43:45,000 --> 00:43:50,000
WHERE NOW?

737
00:44:03,000 --> 00:44:08,000
Hastings:
I DON'T SUPPOSE YOU'D CARE
TO TELL ME WHAT'S GOING ON.

738
00:44:10,000 --> 00:44:11,000
YOU KNOW, POIROT

739
00:44:11,000 --> 00:44:15,000
YOU REALLY ARE
QUITE IMPOSSIBLE.

740
00:44:15,000 --> 00:44:16,000
WHY, HASTINGS?

741
00:44:16,000 --> 00:44:18,000
YOU NEVER TELL ME ANYTHING.

742
00:44:18,000 --> 00:44:23,000
I'VE NO IDEA WHERE WE ARE
OR WHERE WE'RE GOING.

743
00:44:24,000 --> 00:44:29,000
HAVE PATIENCE, MON AMI.

744
00:44:29,000 --> 00:44:34,000
SOON ALL WILL
BE MADE CLEAR.

745
00:44:35,000 --> 00:44:36,000
YOU!

746
00:44:36,000 --> 00:44:39,000
MADEMOISELLE, I AM
ONLY TRYING TO HELP YOU.

747
00:44:39,000 --> 00:44:41,000
YOU ARREST
MY FIANCEE.

748
00:44:41,000 --> 00:44:42,000
McNEIL ARRESTS
MR. VAVASOUR.

749
00:44:42,000 --> 00:44:44,000
YOU'RE BOTH AS BAD
AS EACH OTHER.

750
00:44:44,000 --> 00:44:46,000
JE VOUS EN PRIE,
MADEMOISELLE--

751
00:44:46,000 --> 00:44:48,000
HAVE PATIENCE.

752
00:44:48,000 --> 00:44:49,000
WELL?

753
00:44:49,000 --> 00:44:51,000
WHEN YOU CAME TO SEE ME

754
00:44:51,000 --> 00:44:54,000
IT IS BECAUSE YOU WERE AFRAID
OF MONSIEUR RIDGEWAY, NO?

755
00:44:54,000 --> 00:44:57,000
I WAS AFRAID FOR HIM.

756
00:44:57,000 --> 00:44:58,000
NO, MADEMOISELLE.

757
00:44:58,000 --> 00:45:01,000
YOU KNEW HE WAS A
GAMBLER MOST COMPULSIVE.

758
00:45:01,000 --> 00:45:04,000
YOU KNEW OF HIS DEBTS
AND IT WAS FOR THIS REASON

759
00:45:04,000 --> 00:45:05,000
THAT HE SOLD
HIS CAR?

760
00:45:05,000 --> 00:45:07,000
I CAN'T DENY IT, MR. POIROT.

761
00:45:07,000 --> 00:45:09,000
YOU SEEM TO KNOW.

762
00:45:09,000 --> 00:45:10,000
AND YOU WERE
ALSO AFRAID

763
00:45:10,000 --> 00:45:14,000
THAT IF HE WERE ENTRUSTED
WITH THE LIBERTY BONDS

764
00:45:14,000 --> 00:45:16,000
THAT HE WOULD TAKE THEM
AND DISAPPEAR.

765
00:45:16,000 --> 00:45:19,000
YOU WISHED
TO PROTECT HIM,
MADEMOISELLE

766
00:45:19,000 --> 00:45:20,000
AND IT IS FOR THIS REASON

767
00:45:20,000 --> 00:45:23,000
THAT YOU STOLE THE KEY
OF YOUR EMPLOYER.

768
00:45:23,000 --> 00:45:25,000
I DON'T KNOW WHAT YOU MEAN!

769
00:45:25,000 --> 00:45:27,000
PLEASE, DO NOT TRY
TO DECEIVE ME!

770
00:45:27,000 --> 00:45:30,000
I KNOW!

771
00:45:30,000 --> 00:45:35,000
YOU TOOK THE KEY?

772
00:45:35,000 --> 00:45:37,000
BECAUSE YOU WISH TO SAVE
MONSIEUR RIDGEWAY

773
00:45:37,000 --> 00:45:40,000
YOU ARE WILLING
TO LET US BELIEVE

774
00:45:40,000 --> 00:45:42,000
THAT THE KEY THAT OPENED
THE PORTMANTEAU

775
00:45:42,000 --> 00:45:44,000
WAS THE KEY OF YOUR EMPLOYER.

776
00:45:44,000 --> 00:45:46,000
BUT I'M AFRAID,
MADEMOISELLE

777
00:45:46,000 --> 00:45:48,000
THAT WILL NOT WORK

778
00:45:48,000 --> 00:45:53,000
BECAUSE THE KEYS HAVE
NOTHING TO DO WITH IT.

779
00:46:00,000 --> 00:46:04,000
McNeil:
WHY HAVE YOU DRAGGED
ME HERE, MR. POIROT?

780
00:46:04,000 --> 00:46:09,000
I THOUGHT IT MIGHT
BE INSTRUCTIVE FOR YOU,
MONSIEUR McNEIL.

781
00:46:09,000 --> 00:46:14,000
( doorbell rings )

782
00:46:20,000 --> 00:46:21,000
IS IT REALLY TRUE

783
00:46:21,000 --> 00:46:23,000
BOTH MR. VAVASOUR
AND RIDGEWAY ARRESTED?

784
00:46:23,000 --> 00:46:26,000
McNeil:
WELL, ONE OF THEM
STOLE THE BONDS.

785
00:46:26,000 --> 00:46:27,000
NO, NO, NO, NO.

786
00:46:27,000 --> 00:46:28,000
THEY STOLE NOTHING.

787
00:46:28,000 --> 00:46:31,000
INDEED, THERE WAS
NOTHING TO STEAL.

788
00:46:31,000 --> 00:46:35,000
YOU SEE, MONSIEUR McNEIL

789
00:46:35,000 --> 00:46:36,000
THE BONDS
WERE TAKEN

790
00:46:36,000 --> 00:46:38,000
BEFORE THE
QUEEN MARY SAILED.

791
00:46:38,000 --> 00:46:40,000
Hastings:
THAT'S IMPOSSIBLE.

792
00:46:40,000 --> 00:46:43,000
WE WERE WITH
THE PORTMANTEAU
L THE TIME.

793
00:46:43,000 --> 00:46:44,000
PAS DU TOUT, MON AMI.

794
00:46:44,000 --> 00:46:48,000
MONSIEUR VAVASOUR, HE PUT
THE BONDS INTO THE PORTMANTEAU

795
00:46:48,000 --> 00:46:51,000
AND THE EYESIGHT OF
MONSIEUR VAVASOUR IS POOR.

796
00:46:51,000 --> 00:46:53,000
HE TOLD US SO HIMSELF.

797
00:46:53,000 --> 00:46:56,000
ONE MILLION DOLLARS
IN LIBERTY BONDS.

798
00:46:56,000 --> 00:46:59,000
Poirot:
NO, HE WOULD NOT HAVE NOTICED

799
00:46:59,000 --> 00:47:04,000
THAT THE BONDS THAT HE
WAS HOLDING WERE ALL FORGERIES.

800
00:47:04,000 --> 00:47:05,000
FORGERIES?

801
00:47:05,000 --> 00:47:07,000
Hastings:
YOU MEAN
THE BONDS

802
00:47:07,000 --> 00:47:09,000
ON THE QUEEN MARY
WERE FAKES?

803
00:47:09,000 --> 00:47:10,000
EXACTLY, MON AMI.

804
00:47:10,000 --> 00:47:11,000
McNeil:
BUT WHY?

805
00:47:11,000 --> 00:47:13,000
WHAT GOOD WOULD THAT DO ANYONE?

806
00:47:13,000 --> 00:47:15,000
MR. SHAW'S GOT
TO REST NOW.

807
00:47:15,000 --> 00:47:18,000
AH, YES, OF COURSE.

808
00:47:18,000 --> 00:47:21,000
HASTINGS.

809
00:47:21,000 --> 00:47:26,000
NURSE LONG, PARDON,
BUT WHAT IS THE TIME?

810
00:47:26,000 --> 00:47:29,000
IT'S TEN PAST 4:00.

811
00:47:29,000 --> 00:47:33,000
C'EST CA.

812
00:47:33,000 --> 00:47:36,000
MADEMOISELLE, PARDON, BUT...

813
00:47:36,000 --> 00:47:41,000
WHAT IS THE TIME?

814
00:47:41,000 --> 00:47:43,000
IT'S JUST 9:30.

815
00:47:43,000 --> 00:47:48,000
ON THE SHIP ALSO I ASKED
YOU THE SAME QUESTION.

816
00:47:49,000 --> 00:47:51,000
THE DISGUISE WAS
TO PERFECTION

817
00:47:51,000 --> 00:47:54,000
BUT THE MOVEMENT WAS
EXACTLY THE SAME.

818
00:47:54,000 --> 00:47:57,000
IT WAS THE MOVEMENT
OF AN EXPERIENCED NURSE

819
00:47:57,000 --> 00:48:02,000
WHO ALWAYS WEARS THE WATCH
ON HER CHEST.

820
00:48:03,000 --> 00:48:04,000
MIRANDA?

821
00:48:04,000 --> 00:48:07,000
MADEMOISELLE BROOKS
OR MADEMOISELLE LONG

822
00:48:07,000 --> 00:48:10,000
WHO TRAVELED WITH A COPY
OF ONE OF THE KEYS

823
00:48:10,000 --> 00:48:13,000
WHO STOLE THE BONDS
THAT WERE FAKE

824
00:48:13,000 --> 00:48:15,000
AND WHO DISPOSED OF THEM.

825
00:48:15,000 --> 00:48:18,000
I DON'T KNOW WHAT
YOU'RE TALKING ABOUT.

826
00:48:18,000 --> 00:48:19,000
SHE CAN'T BE.

827
00:48:19,000 --> 00:48:22,000
MIRANDA BROOKS WAS A STUNNER.

828
00:48:22,000 --> 00:48:24,000
RIDGEWAY WOULD
TAKE THE BLAME.

829
00:48:24,000 --> 00:48:26,000
WITH THE PROBLEMS
OF HIS GAMBLING

830
00:48:26,000 --> 00:48:29,000
HE WOULD BE
THE OBVIOUS SUSPECT.

831
00:48:29,000 --> 00:48:31,000
HE WOULD BECOME
THE... SCAPEGOAT.

832
00:48:31,000 --> 00:48:32,000
HE DID STEAL THEM.

833
00:48:32,000 --> 00:48:34,000
HE WAS TRAVELING
WITH THEM.

834
00:48:34,000 --> 00:48:36,000
PRECISELY WHAT YOU
ARE INTENDED TO THINK.

835
00:48:36,000 --> 00:48:38,000
THAT WAS WHY
IT WAS ESSENTIAL

836
00:48:38,000 --> 00:48:41,000
THAT MONSIEUR RIDGEWAY
SHOULD BE ON THAT BOAT.

837
00:48:41,000 --> 00:48:43,000
IT WAS
MADEMOISELLE BROOKS

838
00:48:43,000 --> 00:48:45,000
WHO TRIED TO KILL
MONSIEUR SHAW

839
00:48:45,000 --> 00:48:49,000
WITH THE MOTOR CAR.

840
00:48:49,000 --> 00:48:54,000
IT WAS MADEMOISELLE BROOKS
WHO ARRANGED THE POISONING.

841
00:48:54,000 --> 00:48:59,000
MIRANDA PLANNED ALL THAT?

842
00:48:59,000 --> 00:49:03,000
ALL RIGHT, YES.

843
00:49:03,000 --> 00:49:07,000
HERE YOU ARE.

844
00:49:07,000 --> 00:49:11,000
GOOD LORD!

845
00:49:11,000 --> 00:49:13,000
WHAT ARE YOU GOING TO DO?

846
00:49:13,000 --> 00:49:16,000
CALL THE POLICE?

847
00:49:16,000 --> 00:49:19,000
ALL RIGHT, LET'S GET ON WITH IT.

848
00:49:19,000 --> 00:49:21,000
NO, NO, NO, NO, NO,
MADEMOISELLE

849
00:49:21,000 --> 00:49:25,000
ONE STEP AT A TIME.

850
00:49:25,000 --> 00:49:27,000
YOU SEE, MADEMOISELLE BROOKS

851
00:49:27,000 --> 00:49:30,000
SHE NOW MAKES
THE ATTEMPT GALLANT

852
00:49:30,000 --> 00:49:32,000
TO SHIELD HER ACCOMPLICE.

853
00:49:32,000 --> 00:49:35,000
RIDGEWAY.

854
00:49:35,000 --> 00:49:37,000
NO...

855
00:49:37,000 --> 00:49:39,000
HOW SIMPLE IT WOULD HAVE BEEN

856
00:49:39,000 --> 00:49:41,000
FOR MONSIEUR SHAW
TO REMOVE THOSE BONDS

857
00:49:41,000 --> 00:49:43,000
THAT WERE
ENTRUSTED TO HIM

858
00:49:43,000 --> 00:49:46,000
IF HE HAD TAKEN THEM
ON BOARD THE BOAT, EH?

859
00:49:46,000 --> 00:49:48,000
TOO SIMPLE, TOO OBVIOUS.

860
00:49:48,000 --> 00:49:51,000
THE BANK WOULD HAVE KNOWN
PRECISELY WHERE TO LOOK.

861
00:49:51,000 --> 00:49:53,000
ARE YOU IMPLYING THAT I WAS

862
00:49:53,000 --> 00:49:55,000

IN SOME WAY
INVOLVED?

863
00:49:55,000 --> 00:49:57,000
I WAS BEDRIDDEN.

864
00:49:57,000 --> 00:50:00,000
YES, OF COURSE YOU WERE,
MONSIEUR SHAW

865
00:50:00,000 --> 00:50:02,000
WITH THE POISON...

866
00:50:02,000 --> 00:50:04,000
THAT WAS FAKE

867
00:50:04,000 --> 00:50:06,000
AS WAS THE ATTEMPT
TO KILL YOU

868
00:50:06,000 --> 00:50:08,000
WITH A MOTOR CAR.

869
00:50:08,000 --> 00:50:09,000
IT WAS PART OF YOUR PLAN

870
00:50:09,000 --> 00:50:12,000
TO GET RIDGEWAY
TO TAKE YOUR PLACE ON THE BOAT.

871
00:50:12,000 --> 00:50:15,000
BUT MR. SHAW
STILL HAD HIS KEY.

872
00:50:15,000 --> 00:50:16,000
NO, NO, NO.

873
00:50:16,000 --> 00:50:18,000
HE HAD A COPY OF HIS KEY.

874
00:50:18,000 --> 00:50:20,000
MADEMOISELLE
BROOKS--

875
00:50:20,000 --> 00:50:24,000
SHE HAD THE REAL ONE.

876
00:50:24,000 --> 00:50:29,000
OH, GOD.

877
00:50:33,000 --> 00:50:37,000
I'M SORRY,
MIRANDA.

878
00:50:37,000 --> 00:50:38,000
YOU ARE HUSBAND
AND WIFE?

879
00:50:38,000 --> 00:50:40,000
NO.

880
00:50:40,000 --> 00:50:44,000
BUT WE INTENDED
TO BE.

881
00:50:44,000 --> 00:50:47,000
I'M SORRY.

882
00:50:47,000 --> 00:50:48,000
DON'T BE.

883
00:50:48,000 --> 00:50:50,000
PRISON CAN'T BE
MUCH WORSE

884
00:50:50,000 --> 00:50:55,000
THAN 25 YEARS
AT THE LONDON
AND SCOTTISH BANK.

885
00:51:00,000 --> 00:51:05,000
COME ON, RIDGEWAY, YOU'RE DONE.

886
00:51:05,000 --> 00:51:10,000
WHERE'S McNEIL?

887
00:51:12,000 --> 00:51:14,000
Ridgeway:
I DON'T SEE WHY

888
00:51:14,000 --> 00:51:16,000
YOU HAD TO HAVE
ME ARRESTED.

889
00:51:16,000 --> 00:51:18,000
BECAUSE I SAW
THE LOAN SHARKS

890
00:51:18,000 --> 00:51:20,000
WAITING FOR YOU
AT SOUTHAMPTON.

891
00:51:20,000 --> 00:51:22,000
I THOUGHT YOU'D
BE SAFER

892
00:51:22,000 --> 00:51:23,000
IN THE
POLICE CELL.

893
00:51:23,000 --> 00:51:25,000
THAT'S TRUE.

894
00:51:25,000 --> 00:51:27,000
IT ALSO ALLOWED
THE REAL CULPRITS

895
00:51:27,000 --> 00:51:29,000
TO RELAX THEIR
GUARD A LITTLE.

896
00:51:29,000 --> 00:51:31,000
I CAN'T TELL YOU
HOW MUCH WE OWE YOU.

897
00:51:31,000 --> 00:51:32,000
I'VE BEEN PROMOTED

898
00:51:32,000 --> 00:51:34,000
TO JOINT
GENERAL MANAGER.

899
00:51:34,000 --> 00:51:36,000
I'VE PAID OFF
MY DEBTS...

900
00:51:36,000 --> 00:51:38,000
AND THERE WON'T
BE ANY MORE.

901
00:51:38,000 --> 00:51:41,000
THANK YOU
FOR EVERYTHING.

902
00:51:41,000 --> 00:51:42,000
GOOD-BYE.

903
00:51:42,000 --> 00:51:47,000
GOOD-BYE.

904
00:51:49,000 --> 00:51:54,000
AU REVOIR.

905
00:51:57,000 --> 00:52:02,000
WE DESERVE TO CELEBRATE
A LITTLE, EH, HASTINGS?

906
00:52:02,000 --> 00:52:06,000
A GLASS OF CREME DE MENTHE?

907
00:52:06,000 --> 00:52:09,000
AH! YOU SCORN
THE LIQUEUR, HASTINGS.

908
00:52:09,000 --> 00:52:13,000
ALORS, FOR YOU, MY FRIEND,
A WHISKEY, PERHAPS?

909
00:52:13,000 --> 00:52:15,000
UH, NO...
NO, THANKS.

910
00:52:15,000 --> 00:52:19,000
HASTINGS... YOU ARE NOT
ELATED BY OUR SUCCESS?

911
00:52:19,000 --> 00:52:21,000
OH, YES, YES,
VERY GOOD.

912
00:52:21,000 --> 00:52:24,000
NE PAS ENCORE
LE MAL DE MER?

913
00:52:24,000 --> 00:52:25,000
NO, I'M FINE.

914
00:52:25,000 --> 00:52:29,000
HASTINGS, WE HAVE
JUST COMPLETED A CASE
MOST SUCCESSFUL.

915
00:52:29,000 --> 00:52:30,000
TWO MEN HAVE BEEN RELEASED

916
00:52:30,000 --> 00:52:33,000
FROM THEMPRISONMENT
MOST UNJUST.

917
00:52:33,000 --> 00:52:36,000
YOU HAVE BEEN PRIVILEGED
TO WATCH HERCULE POIROT

918
00:52:36,000 --> 00:52:37,000
AT HIS MOST BRILLIANT.

919
00:52:37,000 --> 00:52:40,000
YOU HAVE HAD THE NICE RIDE
ON THE QUEEN MARY.

920
00:52:40,000 --> 00:52:44,000
WELL, I... I KNOW, POIROT,
I... I'M SORRY.

921
00:52:44,000 --> 00:52:46,000
IT'S MIRANDA BROOKS.

922
00:52:46,000 --> 00:52:49,000
AH, HASTINGS.

923
00:52:49,000 --> 00:52:51,000
YOU STILL HAVE THE HANKERING

924
00:52:51,000 --> 00:52:54,000
FOR THE GLAMOROUS
YOUNG WOMAN, EH?

925
00:52:54,000 --> 00:52:56,000
NO, NO, NO, NO, NOT AT ALL.

926
00:52:56,000 --> 00:52:59,000
NO, QUITE THE OPPOSITE,
IN FACT.

927
00:52:59,000 --> 00:53:01,000
IT'S JUST THAT...

928
00:53:01,000 --> 00:53:05,000
WELL, THERE SHE WAS, AS YOU SAY,
A GLAMOROUS YOUNG WOMAN.

929
00:53:05,000 --> 00:53:06,000
WITH A BIT
OF A WIG

930
00:53:06,000 --> 00:53:08,000
AND A FEW BITS
OF MAKEUP

931
00:53:08,000 --> 00:53:13,000
SHE COULD TRANSFORM HERSELF
INTO THAT DOWDY HAG OF A NURSE.

932
00:53:13,000 --> 00:53:15,000
IT WAS VERY WELL DONE, HASTINGS.

933
00:53:15,000 --> 00:53:19,000
BUT... WELL, I MEAN...

934
00:53:19,000 --> 00:53:24,000
IF A WOMAN CAN DO THAT ONE WAY,
SHE CAN DO IT THE OTHER.

935
00:53:24,000 --> 00:53:26,000
AH, HASTINGS.

936
00:53:26,000 --> 00:53:28,000
WELL...

937
00:53:28,000 --> 00:53:33,000
I MEAN, THEN WHERE ARE YOU?

938
00:53:33,000 --> 00:53:38,000
AT THE BEGINNING OF WISDOM,
MON AMI.

939
00:53:40,000 --> 00:53:44,000

NOW THAT ALSO IS
SOMETHING TO CELEBRATE

940
00:53:44,000 --> 00:53:49,000

N'EST CE PAS?

941
00:55:12,000 --> 00:55:17,000
CAPTIONS COPYRIGHT LONDON
WEEKEND TELEVISION INTERNATIONAL

942
00:55:24,000 --> 00:55:28,000
CHRISTIE'S FIRST BOOK INTRODUCES
HERCULE POIROT

943
00:55:28,000 --> 00:55:32,000
AND HER NAME WILL BE ASSOCIATED
WITH HIS FOREVER.

944
00:55:32,000 --> 00:55:36,000
HE IS HER MOST FAMOUS DETECTIVE,
AND MOST OF HER...

945
00:55:36,000 --> 00:55:41,000
A GREAT NUMBER OF HER BEST BOOKS
FEATURE HIM AS THE DETECTIVE.

946
00:55:41,000 --> 00:55:46,000
YET, STRANGELY, SHE HAS A VERY
CONFLICTING ATTITUDE TOWARD HIM.

947
00:55:46,000 --> 00:55:48,000
SHE DOESN'T LIKE HIM.

948
00:55:48,000 --> 00:55:51,000
YET, THE FIRST BOOK
HAS HIM THERE.

949
00:55:51,000 --> 00:55:52,000
ALL THE TRAITS ALMOST

950
00:55:52,000 --> 00:55:56,000
THAT WE ARE GOING TO
ASSOCIATE WITH POIROT

951
00:55:56,000 --> 00:55:58,000
ARE THERE IN THE FIRST BOOK--

952
00:55:58,000 --> 00:56:02,000
THE PHYSICAL DESCRIPTION
OF HIM, THE MODUS OPERANDI

953
00:56:02,000 --> 00:56:05,000
THE WAY HE GOES ABOUT CRIME

954
00:56:05,000 --> 00:56:07,000
THEY'RE ALL THERE
IN THE FIRST BOOK.

955
00:56:07,000 --> 00:56:12,000
NOW, THE STRANGE THING IS THAT
CHRISTIE CREATES A DETECTIVE

956
00:56:12,000 --> 00:56:15,000
WHO IS THE OPPOSITE OF HERSELF.

957
00:56:15,000 --> 00:56:18,000
MALE DETECTIVE WRITERS
OFTEN CREATE A DETECTIVE

958
00:56:18,000 --> 00:56:22,000
WHO IS IN SOME SENSE
A BIGGER AND BETTER

959
00:56:22,000 --> 00:56:25,000
A LARGER-THAN-LIFE VERSION
OF THEMSELVES

960
00:56:25,000 --> 00:56:28,000
OR SOME PART OF THEIR LIVES.

961
00:56:28,000 --> 00:56:33,000
IF WE LOOK AT POIROT,
HERE HE IS, HE'S SHORT, BALD

962
00:56:34,000 --> 00:56:39,000
ELDERLY, EXCESSIVELY NEAT,
BELGIAN DETECTIVE-- A MAN.

963
00:56:42,000 --> 00:56:43,000
AND WHAT WAS CHRISTIE?

964
00:56:43,000 --> 00:56:47,000
SHE WAS A RATHER TALL,
RATHER BEAUTIFUL WOMAN

965
00:56:47,000 --> 00:56:52,000
ENGLISH, UPPER MIDDLE CLASS,
AND KNOWN TO BE RATHER MESSY.

966
00:56:52,000 --> 00:56:56,000
SHE WAS NOT AN OBSESSIVELY
TIDY WOMAN, SHALL WE SAY.

967
00:56:56,000 --> 00:56:59,000
SO IN A WAY, POIROT IS
THE REVERSE OF HER.

968
00:56:59,000 --> 00:57:02,000
SHE FLIPS HER OWN CHARACTER.

969
00:57:02,000 --> 00:57:05,000
SHE WAS ALSO VERY, VERY QUIET.

970
00:57:05,000 --> 00:57:09,000
SHE DID NOT HAVE
MUCH SOCIAL CONVERSATION.

971
00:57:09,000 --> 00:57:11,000
POIROT HAS LOTS TO SAY.

972
00:57:11,000 --> 00:57:14,000
HE ALWAYS LIKES
TO DOMINATE THE SITUATION.

973
00:57:14,000 --> 00:57:19,000
SO AGAIN, SHE CREATES SOMEONE
WHO'S THE OPPOSITE OF HERSELF.

974
00:57:20,000 --> 00:57:23,000
AND THIS WORKED ON SOME LEVEL
EXTREMELY WELL

975
00:57:23,000 --> 00:57:25,000
BUT IT CREATED PROBLEMS

976
00:57:25,000 --> 00:57:30,000
BECAUSE SHE HAS SOMEONE
WHO SHE CANNOT EMPATHIZE WITH

977
00:57:30,000 --> 00:57:33,000
THAT SHE CAN'T DEVELOP
IN SOME SENSE.

978
00:57:33,000 --> 00:57:35,000
HE FULFILLS NARRATIVE GOALS.

979
00:57:35,000 --> 00:57:40,000
HE SERVES IN HER BOOKS,
AND YET HE'S NOT A REAL PERSON.

980
00:57:40,000 --> 00:57:45,000
MISS MARPLE WILL BECOME MUCH
CLOSER TO CHRISTIE AS A PERSON

981
00:57:45,000 --> 00:57:49,000
BUT POIROT CAN NEVER BE
CLOSE TO HER AS A PERSON.

982
00:57:49,000 --> 00:57:52,000
HE IS ALWAYS...
ALMOST LIKE AN INCARNATION

983
00:57:52,000 --> 00:57:57,000
OF THE COLD, CALCULATING,
DISSOCIATED PART OF CHRISTIE

984
00:57:57,000 --> 00:58:01,000
THE PART THAT SHE WASN'T LIVING
IN HER LIFE.

985
00:58:01,000 --> 00:58:05,000
HE IS THE PERSON WHO IS
ALL BRAIN IN A CERTAIN WAY.

986
00:58:05,000 --> 00:58:07,000
IT'S THE LITTLE GRAY CELLS.

987
00:58:07,000 --> 00:58:11,000
HE IS THE INTELLECTUAL PRINCIPLE
AT WORK IN THE SCENE

988
00:58:11,000 --> 00:58:16,000
AND HIS LIFE... HE HAS NO
PERSONAL LIFE, IN A CERTAIN WAY.

989
00:58:16,000 --> 00:58:18,000
SHE HAD LOTS OF PERSONAL LIFE.

990
00:58:18,000 --> 00:58:21,000
SO THERE WAS
A DIFFICULTY FOR HER

991
00:58:21,000 --> 00:58:25,000
IN CONTINUING TO WRITE
BOOK AFTER BOOK AFTER BOOK

992
00:58:25,000 --> 00:58:27,000
ABOUT THIS PERSON

993
00:58:27,000 --> 00:58:32,000
AND THIS DIFFICULTY CULMINATED
IN THE FACT THAT DURING THE WAR

994
00:58:32,000 --> 00:58:35,000
SHE WRITES THE DEATH OF POIROT

995
00:58:35,000 --> 00:58:38,000
AND THEN PUTS THE BOOK AWAY
IN THE VAULTS

996
00:58:38,000 --> 00:58:41,000
AND IT'S FINALLY PUBLISHED
IN THE 1970s.

997
00:58:41,000 --> 00:58:43,000
BUT SHE MAKES--

998
00:58:43,000 --> 00:58:48,000
SHE HAS CERTAIN PLEASURE
IN IMAGINING HIM DEAD.

999
00:58:51,000 --> 00:58:56,000
