÷B=W:F
CRIME ISSUED A ROYAL DECREE:

1006
01:00:16,000 --> 01:00:17,000
CERTAINLY NOT!

1007
01:00:17,000 --> 01:00:21,000
STILL, EVEN CHRISTIE
COULDN'T RESIST THE URGE

1008
01:00:21,000 --> 01:00:24,000
TO DANGLE A BEAUTIFUL AND CLEVER
WOMAN IN FRONT OF POIROT

1009
01:00:24,000 --> 01:00:27,000
TO SEE HOW HE WOULD REACT.

1010
01:00:27,000 --> 01:00:30,000
AND WHAT A REMARKABLE
WOMAN SHE IS--

1011
01:00:30,000 --> 01:00:34,000
COUNTESS VERA ROSSAKOFF,
AN ARISTOCRATIC RUSSIAN EMIGRE

1012
01:00:34,000 --> 01:00:36,000
DRIVEN FROM HER HOMELAND

1013
01:00:36,000 --> 01:00:40,000
WHEN THE REVOLUTION SWEPT
THE OLD REGIME FROM POWER.

1014
01:00:40,000 --> 01:00:43,000
POIROT FIRST ENCOUNTERS
HER TONIGHT

1015
01:00:43,000 --> 01:00:46,000
WHEN HE INVESTIGATES
A SERIES OF JEWEL THEFTS

1016
01:00:46,000 --> 01:00:51,000
AND QUICKLY FINDS THAT SOMETHING
MORE VALUABLE THAN DIAMONDS

1017
01:00:51,000 --> 01:00:54,000
MAY ALSO BE STOLEN-- HIS HEART.

1018
01:00:54,000 --> 01:00:59,000
"THE DOUBLE CLUE."

1019
01:02:08,000 --> 01:02:12,000
Woman on P.A.:
THE TRAIN NOW ARRIVING
ON PLATFORM ONE

1020
01:02:12,000 --> 01:02:17,000
IS THE 5:30 FROM ILFRACOMBE,
BARNSTABLE, EXETER AND YEOVIL.

1021
01:02:18,000 --> 01:02:21,000
THE TRAIN NOW ARRIVING
ON PLATFORM ONE

1022
01:02:21,000 --> 01:02:26,000
IS THE 5:30 FROM ILFRACOMBE,
BARNSTABLE, EXETER AND YEOVIL.

1023
01:03:05,000 --> 01:03:06,000
      GOOD EVENING, COUNTESS.

1024
01:03:06,000 --> 01:03:09,000
IT'S AN HONOR
TO HAVE YOU
WITH US AGAIN.

1025
01:03:09,000 --> 01:03:14,000
YOUR USUAL
SUITE IS READY.

1026
01:03:35,000 --> 01:03:36,000
THANK YOU.

1027
01:03:36,000 --> 01:03:41,000
THANK YOU,
COUNTESS.

1028
01:03:58,000 --> 01:04:01,000
Hastings:
DOESN'T THE TOWN LOOK GOOD

1029
01:04:01,000 --> 01:04:03,000
AT THIS TIME
OF YEAR, POIROT?

1030
01:04:03,000 --> 01:04:05,000
ONE CAN TELL THE
SUMMER HAS ARRIVED.

1031
01:04:05,000 --> 01:04:07,000
IT'S IN THE AIR, EH?

1032
01:04:07,000 --> 01:04:10,000
NO, IT IS IN THE SPEED
OF YOUR DRIVING.

1033
01:04:10,000 --> 01:04:15,000
COME OFF IT, POIROT,
WE'RE ONLY PUSHING 30.

1034
01:04:19,000 --> 01:04:20,000
( tires squeal )

1035
01:04:20,000 --> 01:04:24,000
SORRY, OLD CHAP--
RED LIGHT.

1036
01:04:24,000 --> 01:04:26,000
I PREFER THE WINTER.

1037
01:04:26,000 --> 01:04:27,000
IT IS SAFER.

1038
01:04:27,000 --> 01:04:31,000
NOW THERE'S A PLEASANT SIGHT
FOR A SUMMER'S DAY.

1039
01:04:31,000 --> 01:04:35,000
HAVE YOU EVER
THOUGHT ABOUT IT?

1040
01:04:35,000 --> 01:04:37,000
IN MY EXPERIENCE I HAVE
KNOWN OF FIVE CASES

1041
01:04:37,000 --> 01:04:40,000
OF WOMEN MURDERED
BY THEIR DEVOTED HUSBANDS.

1042
01:04:40,000 --> 01:04:42,000
YES?

1043
01:04:42,000 --> 01:04:47,000
AND 22 HUSBANDS MURDERED
BY THEIR DEVOTED WIVES.

1044
01:04:47,000 --> 01:04:49,000
SO THANK YOU, NON--

1045
01:04:49,000 --> 01:04:52,000
THE MARRIAGE
IT IS NOT FOR ME.

1046
01:04:52,000 --> 01:04:55,000
AH, AND NOW I THINK
THE LIGHT IT IS GREEN.

1047
01:04:55,000 --> 01:04:57,000
WE CAN PROCEED-- GENTLY.

1048
01:04:57,000 --> 01:05:02,000
RIGHT-O.

1049
01:05:04,000 --> 01:05:06,000
BUT I'M NOT GOING
TO HAVE A CRASH.

1050
01:05:06,000 --> 01:05:08,000
ANYWAY, WE SAW A BRIDE.

1051
01:05:08,000 --> 01:05:10,000
THAT'S SUPPOSED
TO BE GOOD LUCK.

1052
01:05:10,000 --> 01:05:12,000
MR. POIROT,
YOU'RE BACK.

1053
01:05:12,000 --> 01:05:15,000
THE CHIEF INSPECTOR'S
WAITING INSIDE.

1054
01:05:15,000 --> 01:05:16,000
CHIEF INSPECTOR
JAPP-- HERE?

1055
01:05:16,000 --> 01:05:20,000
THAT MUST BE THE LUCK OF
WHICH YOU SPEAK, HASTINGS.

1056
01:05:20,000 --> 01:05:23,000
I THINK HE'S WORRIED
ABOUT SOMETHING.

1057
01:05:23,000 --> 01:05:28,000
HE HASN'T SAID A WORD.

1058
01:05:28,000 --> 01:05:31,000
CHIEF INSPECTOR.

1059
01:05:31,000 --> 01:05:33,000
AFTERNOON, POIROT,
CAPTAIN HASTINGS.

1060
01:05:33,000 --> 01:05:35,000
CHIEF INSPECTOR.

1061
01:05:35,000 --> 01:05:39,000
PLEASE SEAT YOURSELF.

1062
01:05:39,000 --> 01:05:42,000
WHAT MATTER IS IT THAT
BRINGS YOU HERE TODAY?

1063
01:05:42,000 --> 01:05:46,000
THE MATTER OF MY JOB, IF
YOU WANT THE HONEST TRUTH.

1064
01:05:46,000 --> 01:05:48,000
THEY'D NEVER
DISMISS YOU

1065
01:05:48,000 --> 01:05:49,000
WOULD THEY?

1066
01:05:49,000 --> 01:05:52,000
THEY WILL IF I DON'T
GET RESULTS SOON

1067
01:05:52,000 --> 01:05:57,000
CAPTAIN HASTINGS.

1068
01:05:58,000 --> 01:06:01,000
THREE ROBBERIES
IN AS MANY WEEKS.

1069
01:06:01,000 --> 01:06:04,000
JEWELRY EACH TIME.

1070
01:06:04,000 --> 01:06:06,000
THE ATTERTON DIAMONDS
WERE THE FIRST TO GO.

1071
01:06:06,000 --> 01:06:08,000
LADY ATTERTON?

1072
01:06:08,000 --> 01:06:10,000
IN THE WEST COUNTRY?

1073
01:06:10,000 --> 01:06:12,000
IT HAPPENED
DURING DINNER.

1074
01:06:12,000 --> 01:06:16,000
TWO DUKES, A DUCHESS
AND SOME RUSSIAN COUNTESS

1075
01:06:16,000 --> 01:06:18,000
ROUND THE TABLE--
UNUSUAL WITNESSES.

1076
01:06:18,000 --> 01:06:20,000
THE HIGH SOCIETY.

1077
01:06:20,000 --> 01:06:23,000
IT CAN'T GET MUCH HIGHER,
THAT'S THE TROUBLE.

1078
01:06:23,000 --> 01:06:25,000
THE COMMISSIONER'S
COME DOWN ON ME.

1079
01:06:25,000 --> 01:06:27,000
HE WANTS ACTION.

1080
01:06:27,000 --> 01:06:30,000
IF NOT, HE'LL HAVE TO
GIVE THEM A SCAPEGOAT.

1081
01:06:30,000 --> 01:06:31,000
A GOAT?

1082
01:06:31,000 --> 01:06:34,000
ME.

1083
01:06:34,000 --> 01:06:37,000
WHEN WAS THIS LAST ROBBERY?

1084
01:06:37,000 --> 01:06:38,000
THREE DAYS AGO.

1085
01:06:38,000 --> 01:06:41,000
THREE DAYS? BUT IT IS TOO LATE.

1086
01:06:41,000 --> 01:06:46,000
IT IS BETTER TO STRIKE WHILE
THE METAL IS WARM, YES?

1087
01:06:47,000 --> 01:06:49,000

SO WHAT CAN WE DO?

1088
01:06:49,000 --> 01:06:52,000
WE WAIT.

1089
01:06:52,000 --> 01:06:57,000
ALREADY THE THIEF HE IS
PLANNING HIS NEXT CRIME.

1090
01:06:57,000 --> 01:07:02,000
AND THE NEXT CRIME--
IT WILL BE HIS LAST.

1091
01:07:39,000 --> 01:07:44,000
Man:
THIS WAY, COUNTESS.

1092
01:07:56,000 --> 01:08:00,000
LADY RUNCORN, HOW
GOOD OF YOU TO COME.

1093
01:08:00,000 --> 01:08:03,000
AND HOW EXQUISITE
YOU LOOK.

1094
01:08:03,000 --> 01:08:06,000
YOUR PARTIES ARE ALWAYS
AN EXPERIENCE, MARCUS.

1095
01:08:06,000 --> 01:08:07,000
AND TONIGHT
IS NO EXCEPTION.

1096
01:08:07,000 --> 01:08:10,000
WE HAVE NACORA,
THE PIANIST,
PLAYING FOR US.

1097
01:08:10,000 --> 01:08:12,000
AND YOU KNOW
KATHERINE BIRD?

1098
01:08:12,000 --> 01:08:14,000
THE CONTRALTO?

1099
01:08:14,000 --> 01:08:17,000
MY DEAR MARCUS, ONE CAN'T
GET TICKETS TO HEAR HER

1100
01:08:17,000 --> 01:08:19,000
FOR LOVE OR MONEY!

1101
01:08:19,000 --> 01:08:21,000
NO NEED FOR EITHER.

1102
01:08:21,000 --> 01:08:23,000
AH, HERE'S A COLLEAGUE OF
MINE FROM SOUTH AFRICA.

1103
01:08:23,000 --> 01:08:26,000
MARTIN JOHNSTONE,
LADY RUNCORN.

1104
01:08:26,000 --> 01:08:27,000
HOW DO YOU DO?

1105
01:08:27,000 --> 01:08:28,000
EXCUSE ME.

1106
01:08:28,000 --> 01:08:32,000
ARE YOU ALSO A COLLECTOR,
MR. JOHNSTONE?

1107
01:08:32,000 --> 01:08:33,000
WHAT?

1108
01:08:33,000 --> 01:08:34,000
JEWELRY.

1109
01:08:34,000 --> 01:08:39,000
MR. HARDMAN HAS
A SUPERLATIVE COLLECTION.

1110
01:08:40,000 --> 01:08:41,000
LADY RUNCORN HERE?

1111
01:08:41,000 --> 01:08:43,000
YES, I'VE JUST SEEN HER.

1112
01:08:43,000 --> 01:08:44,000
OH, GOOD!

1113
01:08:44,000 --> 01:08:47,000
SHE'S QUITE
ATTRACTIVE, REALLY.

1114
01:08:47,000 --> 01:08:50,000
I WONDER IF SHE MISSES
THE LATE LORD RUNCORN.

1115
01:08:50,000 --> 01:08:54,000
FOR HEAVEN'S SAKE,
DO TRY TO BE DISCREET.

1116
01:08:54,000 --> 01:08:56,000
YOU KNOW ME, MARCUS.

1117
01:08:56,000 --> 01:09:00,000
YES...

1118
01:09:00,000 --> 01:09:01,000
WHO'S THAT?

1119
01:09:01,000 --> 01:09:04,000
THE COUNTESS
VERA ROSSAKOFF.

1120
01:09:04,000 --> 01:09:09,000
SHE CAME OVER FROM RUSSIA
QUITE RECENTLY.

1121
01:09:09,000 --> 01:09:11,000
OH, YES.

1122
01:09:11,000 --> 01:09:15,000
I SUGGEST YOU KEEP YOUR
HANDS OFF HER, DEAR BOY.

1123
01:09:15,000 --> 01:09:17,000
WHY?

1124
01:09:17,000 --> 01:09:21,000
YOU'RE NOT IN HER LEAGUE.

1125
01:09:21,000 --> 01:09:26,000
I WONDER.

1126
